{"about":"Sobre: Leal súdito do rei, serve o com total dedicação. Melhor cavaleiro e espadachim do reino, tem um passado trágico que o deixou desfigurado, por isso usa uma máscara de ferro.","advantages":[],"alignmentName":"LAWFUL_EVIL","allRequiredClasses":{"jobs":["{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"archetypeSelectionLevel\":3,\"archetypes\":[{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You choose to gain proficiency in either the Arcana or the Nature skill, and you choose to learn either the Prestidigitation or the Druidcraft cantrip\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Customea0a9569-73a8-44fc-a6af-eb9a3e60a900\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Arcane Archer Lore\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you gain this feature, you learn 2 Arcane Shot options of your choice. Once per turn, when you fire an arrow from a shortbow or longbow as part of the Attack action, you can apply one of your Arcane Shot options to that arrow. You decide to use the option when the arrow hits a creature, unless the option doesn\\u0027t involve an attack roll. You have two uses of this ability, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":3},{\"description\":\"When you gain this feature, you learn 3 Arcane Shot options of your choice. Once per turn, when you fire an arrow from a shortbow or longbow as part of the Attack action, you can apply one of your Arcane Shot options to that arrow. You decide to use the option when the arrow hits a creature, unless the option doesn\\u0027t involve an attack roll. You have two uses of this ability, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":7},{\"description\":\"When you gain this feature, you learn 4 Arcane Shot options of your choice. Once per turn, when you fire an arrow from a shortbow or longbow as part of the Attack action, you can apply one of your Arcane Shot options to that arrow. You decide to use the option when the arrow hits a creature, unless the option doesn\\u0027t involve an attack roll. You have two uses of this ability, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"When you gain this feature, you learn 5 Arcane Shot options of your choice. Once per turn, when you fire an arrow from a shortbow or longbow as part of the Attack action, you can apply one of your Arcane Shot options to that arrow. You decide to use the option when the arrow hits a creature, unless the option doesn\\u0027t involve an attack roll. You have two uses of this ability, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":15},{\"description\":\"When you gain this feature, you learn 6 Arcane Shot options of your choice. Once per turn, when you fire an arrow from a shortbow or longbow as part of the Attack action, you can apply one of your Arcane Shot options to that arrow. You decide to use the option when the arrow hits a creature, unless the option doesn\\u0027t involve an attack roll. You have two uses of this ability, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a short or long rest. Each option also improves when you become an 18th-level fighter\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom29aa1bb8-16f7-40fd-a2a8-fe514d8f597f\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Arcane Shot\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Whenever you fire a nonmagical arrow from a shortbow or longbow, you can make it magical for the purpose of overcoming resistance and immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage. The magic fades from the arrow immediately after it hits or misses its target\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Custom1063d6cc-b38b-47ab-a7f8-3395532794ad\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Magic Arrow\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you make an attack roll with a magic arrow and miss, you can use a bonus action to reroll the attack roll against a different target within 60 feet of the original target\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Custom6ac4d916-2f9a-4b8b-a92c-3058c5913913\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Curving Shot\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"If you roll initiative and have no uses of Arcane Shot remaining, you regain one use of it\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Customac551e2a-1fae-4f48-abea-178f5fc6af13\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Ever-Ready Shot\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"The options are all magical effects. If an option requires a saving throw, your Arcane Shot save DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Intelligence modifier.\\n\\n- Banishing Arrow: The creature hit by the arrow must also succeed on a Charisma saving throw or be banished. While banished in this way, the target\\u0027s speed is 0, and it is incapacitated. At the end of its next turn, the target reappears in the space it vacated or in the nearest unoccupied space if that space is occupied. After you reach 18th level in this class, a target also takes 2d6 force damage when the arrow hits it.\\n\\n- Beguiling Arrow: The creature hit by the arrow takes an extra 2d6 psychic damage, and choose one of your allies within 30 feet of the target. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw, or it is charmed by the chosen ally until the start of your next turn. This effect ends early if the chosen ally attacks the charmed target, deals damage to it, or forces it to make a saving throw. The psychic damage increases to 4d6 when you reach 18th level in this class.\\n\\n- Bursting Arrow: Immediately after the arrow hits the creature, the target and all other creatures within 10 feet of it take 2d6 force damage each. The force damage increases to 4d6 when you reach 18th level in this class.\\n\\n- Enfeebling Arrow: The creature hit by the arrow takes an extra 2d6 necrotic damage. The target must also succeed on a Constitution saving throw, or the damage dealt by its weapon attacks is halved until the start of your next turn. The necrotic damage increases to 4d6 when you reach 18th level in this class.\\n\\n- Grasping Arrow: The creature hit by the arrow is wreathed in brambles and takes an extra 2d6 poison damage, its speed is reduced by 10 feet, and it takes 2d6 slashing damage the first time on each turn it moves 1 foot or more without teleporting. The target or any creature that can reach it can use its action to remove the brambles with a successful Strength (Athletics) check against your Arcane Shot save DC. Otherwise, the brambles last for 1 minute or until you use this option again. The poison damage and slashing damage both increase to 4d6 when you reach 18th level in this class.\\n\\n- Piercing Arrow: When you use this option, you don\\u0027t make an attack roll for the attack. Instead, the arrow shoots forward in a line, which is 1 foot wide and 30 feet long, before disappearing. The arrow passes harmlessly through objects, ignoring cover. Each creature in that line must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes damage as if it were hit by the arrow, plus an extra 1d6 piercing damage. On a successful save, a target takes half as much damage. The piercing damage increases to 2d6 when you reach 18th level in this class.\\n\\n- Seeking Arrow: When you use this option, you don\\u0027t make an attack roll for the attack. Instead, choose one creature you have seen in the past minute. The arrow flies toward that creature, moving around corners if necessary and ignoring three-quarters cover and half cover. If the target is within the weapon\\u0027s range and there is a path large enough for the arrow to travel to the target, the target must make a Dexterity saving throw. Otherwise, the arrow disappears after traveling as far as it can. On a failed save, the target takes damage as if it were hit by the arrow, plus an extra 1d6 force damage, and you learn the target\\u0027s current location. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage, and you don\\u0027t learn its location. The force damage increases to 2d6 when you reach 18th level in this class.\\n\\n- Shadow Arrow: The creature hit by the arrow takes an extra 2d6 psychic damage, and it must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or be unable to see anything farther than 5 feet away until the start of your next turn. The psychic damage increases to 4d6 when you reach 18th level in this class\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Customd2a7aeab-5e6d-4a79-862a-9c7eeaf88b97\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Arcane Shot Options\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter_arcane_archer\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Arcane Archer\",\"selectableFeatures\":[{\"amountsPerLevel\":[{\"amount\":2,\"level\":3},{\"amount\":3,\"level\":7},{\"amount\":4,\"level\":10},{\"amount\":5,\"level\":15},{\"amount\":6,\"level\":18}],\"availableFeatures\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"The creature hit by the arrow must also succeed on a Charisma saving throw or be banished. While banished in this way, the target\\u0027s speed is 0, and it is incapacitated. At the end of its next turn, the target reappears in the space it vacated or in the nearest unoccupied space if that space is occupied. After you reach 18th level in this class, a target also takes 2d6 force damage when the arrow hits it\",\"level\":1},{\"description\":\"The creature hit by the arrow takes 2d6 force damage and must also succeed on a Charisma saving throw or be banished. While banished in this way, the target\\u0027s speed is 0, and it is incapacitated. At the end of its next turn, the target reappears in the space it vacated or in the nearest unoccupied space if that space is occupied\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom93d33e55-9aaa-462e-95a1-668588915f23\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Banishing Arrow\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"The creature hit by the arrow takes an extra 2d6 psychic damage, and choose one of your allies within 30 feet of the target. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw, or it is charmed by the chosen ally until the start of your next turn. This effect ends early if the chosen ally attacks the charmed target, deals damage to it, or forces it to make a saving throw\",\"level\":1},{\"description\":\"The creature hit by the arrow takes an extra 4d6 psychic damage, and choose one of your allies within 30 feet of the target. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw, or it is charmed by the chosen ally until the start of your next turn. This effect ends early if the chosen ally attacks the charmed target, deals damage to it, or forces it to make a saving throw\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom7eb178a2-d819-4bbd-a2ec-18afad4cd06d\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Beguiling Arrow\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Immediately after the arrow hits the creature, the target and all other creatures within 10 feet of it take 2d6 force damage each\",\"level\":1},{\"description\":\"Immediately after the arrow hits the creature, the target and all other creatures within 10 feet of it take 4d6 force damage each\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom57493e5e-806e-4c50-8f5d-570ae9b82d44\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Bursting Arrow\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"The creature hit by the arrow takes an extra 2d6 necrotic damage. The target must also succeed on a Constitution saving throw, or the damage dealt by its weapon attacks is halved until the start of your next turn\",\"level\":1},{\"description\":\"The creature hit by the arrow takes an extra 4d6 necrotic damage. The target must also succeed on a Constitution saving throw, or the damage dealt by its weapon attacks is halved until the start of your next turn\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custombb5d8b82-e037-4576-bdd1-7fe9698d868b\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Enfeebling Arrow\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"The creature hit by the arrow is wreathed in brambles and takes an extra 2d6 poison damage, its speed is reduced by 10 feet, and it takes 2d6 slashing damage the first time on each turn it moves 1 foot or more without teleporting. The target or any creature that can reach it can use its action to remove the brambles with a successful Strength (Athletics) check against your Arcane Shot save DC. Otherwise, the brambles last for 1 minute or until you use this option again\",\"level\":1},{\"description\":\"The creature hit by the arrow is wreathed in brambles and takes an extra 4d6 poison damage, its speed is reduced by 10 feet, and it takes 4d6 slashing damage the first time on each turn it moves 1 foot or more without teleporting. The target or any creature that can reach it can use its action to remove the brambles with a successful Strength (Athletics) check against your Arcane Shot save DC. Otherwise, the brambles last for 1 minute or until you use this option again\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom9f0095a2-d2b1-410f-b1c4-84d6b6453ad6\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Grasping Arrow\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you use this option, you don\\u0027t make an attack roll for the attack. Instead, the arrow shoots forward in a line, which is 1 foot wide and 30 feet long, before disappearing. The arrow passes harmlessly through objects, ignoring cover. Each creature in that line must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes damage as if it were hit by the arrow, plus an extra 1d6 piercing damage. On a successful save, a target takes half as much damage\",\"level\":1},{\"description\":\"When you use this option, you don\\u0027t make an attack roll for the attack. Instead, the arrow shoots forward in a line, which is 1 foot wide and 30 feet long, before disappearing. The arrow passes harmlessly through objects, ignoring cover. Each creature in that line must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes damage as if it were hit by the arrow, plus an extra 2d6 piercing damage. On a successful save, a target takes half as much damage\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Customcbaa5403-8b71-4b68-87de-bb6f5984d3ef\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Piercing Arrow\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you use this option, you don\\u0027t make an attack roll for the attack. Instead, choose one creature you have seen in the past minute. The arrow flies toward that creature, moving around corners if necessary and ignoring three-quarters cover and half cover. If the target is within the weapon\\u0027s range and there is a path large enough for the arrow to travel to the target, the target must make a Dexterity saving throw. Otherwise, the arrow disappears after traveling as far as it can. On a failed save, the target takes damage as if it were hit by the arrow, plus an extra 1d6 force damage, and you learn the target\\u0027s current location. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage, and you don\\u0027t learn its location\",\"level\":1},{\"description\":\"When you use this option, you don\\u0027t make an attack roll for the attack. Instead, choose one creature you have seen in the past minute. The arrow flies toward that creature, moving around corners if necessary and ignoring three-quarters cover and half cover. If the target is within the weapon\\u0027s range and there is a path large enough for the arrow to travel to the target, the target must make a Dexterity saving throw. Otherwise, the arrow disappears after traveling as far as it can. On a failed save, the target takes damage as if it were hit by the arrow, plus an extra 2d6 force damage, and you learn the target\\u0027s current location. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage, and you don\\u0027t learn its location\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Customffd6f9e0-20c5-45d0-b3e3-fb1cef37ecc1\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Seeking Arrow\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"The creature hit by the arrow takes an extra 2d6 psychic damage, and it must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or be unable to see anything farther than 5 feet away until the start of your next turn\",\"level\":1},{\"description\":\"The creature hit by the arrow takes an extra 4d6 psychic damage, and it must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or be unable to see anything farther than 5 feet away until the start of your next turn\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom283db0c6-d8ed-4a29-9af2-a2338d34464e\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Shadow Arrow\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1}],\"canReselect\":false,\"id\":\"915263f5-34d2-4936-859c-e17542fae908\",\"name\":\"Arcane Shot Options\",\"selectedFeatures\":[]}],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[{\"abilityCalculators\":[],\"amountsPerLevel\":[{\"amount\":2,\"associatedValue\":\"2\",\"level\":3},{\"amount\":2,\"associatedValue\":\"3\",\"level\":7},{\"amount\":2,\"associatedValue\":\"4\",\"level\":10},{\"amount\":2,\"associatedValue\":\"5\",\"level\":15},{\"amount\":2,\"associatedValue\":\"6\",\"level\":18}],\"associatedValueName\":\"Shots Known\",\"id\":\"52875393-f3a2-4047-a28d-2c1eaf1dc25a\",\"name\":\"Arcane Shot\",\"type\":\"BASIC\",\"usesLeft\":0}],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You learn 3 special maneuvers. You can use only one maneuver per attack\",\"level\":3},{\"description\":\"You learn 5 special maneuvers. You can use only one maneuver per attack\",\"level\":7},{\"description\":\"You learn 7 special maneuvers. You can use only one maneuver per attack\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"You learn 9 special maneuvers. You can use only one maneuver per attack\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Custom66901977-90dd-423c-814c-b0d494562484\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Combat Superiority: Maneuvers\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You have 4 superiority dice, which are d8s, and you expend one whenever you use a maneuver. You regain them all when you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":3},{\"description\":\"You have 5 superiority dice, which are d8s, and you expend one whenever you use a maneuver. You regain them all when you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":7},{\"description\":\"You have 5 superiority dice, which are d10s, and you expend one whenever you use a maneuver. You regain them all when you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"You have 6 superiority dice, which are d8s, and you expend one whenever you use a maneuver. You regain them all when you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":15},{\"description\":\"You have 6 superiority dice, which are d12s, and you expend one whenever you use a maneuver. You regain them all when you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Customc02c5f44-8070-49e1-b1b9-3deff64a1bf6\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Combat Superiority: Superiority Dice\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Some of your maneuvers require your target to make a saving throw to resist the maneuver\\u0027s effects. The saving throw DC \\u003d 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice)\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custome1149ff4-e8d3-44bf-9d40-acb69c349644\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Combat Superiority: Saving Throws\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain proficiency with one type of artisan\\u0027s tool of your choice\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom930cbe56-0ff6-4d14-85ff-671c68c6a6c8\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Student of War\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"If you spend 1 minute observing or interacting with another creature outside of combat, you can learn certain information about its capabilities compared to your own. The DM tells you if the creature is your equal, superior, or inferior in regard to two of the following characteristics of your choice:\\n\\n- Strength score\\n- Dexterity score\\n- Constitution score\\n- Armor Class\\n- Current hit points\\n- Total class levels (if any)\\n- Fighter class levels (if any)\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Customc275bdbd-4dbe-45d2-9497-c2c2e3888a45\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Know Your Enemy\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Your superiority dice turn into d10\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"your superiority dice turn into d12\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom6ee1b50c-bd67-4507-8783-445b53c3956c\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Improved Combat Superiority\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":10},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Whenever you roll for initiative and have zero superiority dice, you get 1 superiority die back\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Custom82eb908f-b707-4079-b5c3-4d0e0ce9c1da\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Relentless\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"- Commander\\u0027s Strike: When you take the Attack action on your turn, you can forgo one of your attacks and use a bonus action to direct one of your companions to strike. When you do so, choose a friendly creature who can see or hear you and expend one superiority die. That creature can immediately use its reaction to make one weapon attack, adding the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll.\\n\\n- Disarming Attack: When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to disarm the target, forcing it to drop one item of your choice that it\\u0027s holding. You add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll, and the target must make a Strength saving throw. On a failed save, it drops the object you choose. The object lands at its feet.  \\n\\n- Distracting Strike: When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to distract the creature, giving your allies an opening. You add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll. The next attack roll against the target by an attacker other than you has advantage if the attack is made before the start of your next turn.  \\n\\n- Evasive Footwork: When you move on your turn, you can expend a superiority die, adding the total to your AC until you stop moving.  \\n\\n- Feinting Attack: You can expend one superiority die and use a bonus action on your turn to feint, choosing one creature within 5 feet of you as your target. Until the end of the turn, you have advantage on your next attack roll against that creature. If that attack hits, add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll.  \\n\\n- Goading Attack: When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to goad the target into attacking you. You add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll, and the target must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the target has a disadvantage on all attack rolls against targets other than you until the end of your next turn.  \\n\\n- Lunging Attack: When you make a melee weapon attack on your turn, you can expend one superiority die to increase your reach for that attack by 5 feet. If you hit, you add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll.  \\n\\n- Maneuvering Attack: When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to maneuver one of your comrades into a more advantageous position. You add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll, and you choose a friendly creature who can see or hear you. That creature can use its reaction to move up to half its speed without provoking opportunity attacks from the target of your attack.\\n\\n- Menacing Attack: When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to frighten the target. You add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll, and the target must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, it is frightened of you until the end of your next turn.  \\n\\n- Parry: When another creature damages you with a melee attack, you can use your reaction and expend one superiority die to reduce the damage by the number you roll on your superiority die + your Dexterity modifier.  \\n\\n- Precision Attack: When you make a weapon attack roll against a creature, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the roll. You can use this maneuver before or after making the attack roll, but before any effects of the attack are applied.  \\n\\n- Pushing Attack: When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to drive the target back. You add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll, and if the target is Large or smaller, it must make a Strength saving throw. On a failed save, you push the target up to 15 feet away from you.  \\n\\n- Rally: On your turn, you can use a bonus action and expend one superiority die to bolster the resolve of one of your companions. When you do so, choose a friendly creature who can see or hear you. That creature gains temporary hit points equal to the superiority die roll + your Charisma modifier.  \\n\\n- Riposte: When a creature misses you with a melee attack, you can use your reaction and expend one superiority die to make a melee attack against the creature. If you hit, you add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll.  \\n\\n- Sweeping Attack: When you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to damage another creature with the same attack. Choose another creature within 5 feet of the original target and within your reach. If the original attack roll would hit the second creature, it takes damage equal to the number you roll on your superiority die. The damage is of the same type dealt by the original attack.  \\n\\n- Trip Attack: When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to knock the target down. You add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll, and if the target is Large or smaller, it must make a Strength saving throw or be knocked prone\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom4a25ac63-4805-4832-8a26-33a26361e97b\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Maneuvers\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter_battle_master\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Battle Master\",\"selectableFeatures\":[{\"amountsPerLevel\":[{\"amount\":3,\"level\":3},{\"amount\":5,\"level\":7},{\"amount\":7,\"level\":10},{\"amount\":9,\"level\":15}],\"availableFeatures\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you take the Attack action on your turn, you can forgo one of your attacks and use a bonus action to direct one of your companions to strike. When you do so, choose a friendly creature who can see or hear you and expend one superiority die. That creature can immediately use its reaction to make one weapon attack, adding the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom91c3c799-fc57-47f7-a0fc-e992de423160\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Commander\\u0027s Strike\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to disarm the target, forcing it to drop one item of your choice that it\\u0027s holding. You add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll, and the target must make a Strength saving throw. On a failed save, it drops the object you choose. The object lands at its feet\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom455d99e9-3efb-4d46-97ab-99b27e45e4a1\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Disarming Attack\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to distract the creature, giving your allies an opening. You add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll. The next attack roll against the target by an attacker other than you has advantage if the attack is made before the start of your next turn\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customf748365b-4286-409d-a413-4971ad01f377\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Distracting Strike\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you move on your turn, you can expend a superiority die, adding the total to your AC until you stop moving\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customfdbf921b-fa2f-4659-920e-44e31a21b438\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Evasive Footwork\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can expend one superiority die and use a bonus action on your turn to feint, choosing one creature within 5 feet of you as your target. Until the end of the turn, you have advantage on your next attack roll against that creature. If that attack hits, add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customd176067b-d396-4d21-81bc-6f0aa7c023a5\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Feinting Attack\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to goad the target into attacking you. You add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll, and the target must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the target has a disadvantage on all attack rolls against targets other than you until the end of your next turn\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom55c1b13e-ae76-46d3-8d2c-11e7d666cadf\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Goading Attack\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you make a melee weapon attack on your turn, you can expend one superiority die to increase your reach for that attack by 5 feet. If you hit, you add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customa96f8c69-1ff7-4408-8edb-5ae1f6fac6ad\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Lunging Attack\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to maneuver one of your comrades into a more advantageous position. You add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll, and you choose a friendly creature who can see or hear you. That creature can use its reaction to move up to half its speed without provoking opportunity attacks from the target of your attack\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom92e386c9-da29-4efb-afc2-7f9f1b704871\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Maneuvering Attack\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to frighten the target. You add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll, and the target must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, it is frightened of you until the end of your next turn\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customc45bd1c9-7a71-4ffc-b233-7c01b3f41f52\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Menacing Attack\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When another creature damages you with a melee attack, you can use your reaction and expend one superiority die to reduce the damage by the number you roll on your superiority die + your Dexterity modifier\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customf8a8e0a8-da01-427b-a10b-62f1c032ce90\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Parry\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you make a weapon attack roll against a creature, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the roll. You can use this maneuver before or after making the attack roll, but before any effects of the attack are applied\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom62fc0003-35ae-4600-afbd-71a23cc7753c\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Precision Attack\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to drive the target back. You add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll, and if the target is Large or smaller, it must make a Strength saving throw. On a failed save, you push the target up to 15 feet away from you\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom388da8f6-26f5-408d-88c4-f3184c041946\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Pushing Attack\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"On your turn, you can use a bonus action and expend one superiority die to bolster the resolve of one of your companions. When you do so, choose a friendly creature who can see or hear you. That creature gains temporary hit points equal to the superiority die roll + your Charisma modifier\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom1e695103-d2e3-49b5-9e73-db388c2adc1b\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Rally\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When a creature misses you with a melee attack, you can use your reaction and expend one superiority die to make a melee attack against the creature. If you hit, you add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customd754708f-caef-4bd0-b579-7e33c82c6f04\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Riposte\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to damage another creature with the same attack. Choose another creature within 5 feet of the original target and within your reach. If the original attack roll would hit the second creature, it takes damage equal to the number you roll on your superiority die. The damage is of the same type dealt by the original attack\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom83883398-d5ac-49cc-8105-b5898f002fab\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Sweeping Attack\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to knock the target down. You add the superiority die to the attack\\u0027s damage roll, and if the target is Large or smaller, it must make a Strength saving throw or be knocked prone\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customc134009f-723c-4c07-af6f-2512dbb5f14f\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Trip Attack\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you make a Dexterity (Stealth) check or an initiative roll, you can expend one superiority die and add the die to the roll, provided you aren\\u0027t incapacitated\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customcc9897ee-a8d4-4cb6-8a63-f88f52b0ebd9\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Ambush\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you\\u0027re within 5 feet of a creature on your turn, you can expend one superiority die and switch places with that creature, provided you spend at least 5 feet of movement and the creature is willing and isn\\u0027t incapacitated. This movement doesn\\u0027t provoke opportunity attacks.\\n\\nRoll the superiority die. Until the start of your next turn, you or the other creature (your choice) gains a bonus to AC equal to the number rolled\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customf5d13156-c432-4846-a469-e2f8a81d06bc\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Bait and Switch\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When a creature you can see moves into the reach you have with the melee weapon you\\u0027re wielding, you can use your reaction to expend one superiority die and make one attack against the creature, using that weapon. If the attack hits, add the superiority die to the weapon\\u0027s damage roll\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customadf13410-eb67-4c5f-943e-9f632fa35831\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Brace\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you make a Charisma (Intimidation), a Charisma (Performance), or a Charisma (Persuasion) check, you can expend one superiority die and add the superiority die to the ability check\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customb7587232-5d33-4086-8755-62f428ccde70\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Commanding Presence\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Immediately after you hit a creature with a melee attack on your turn, you can expend one superiority die and then try to grapple the target as a bonus action (see the Player\\u0027s Handbook for rules on grappling). Add the superiority die to your Strength (Athletics) check\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom195d4c99-a3d1-4a59-82c5-36f53f59ab1a\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Grappling Strike\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"As a bonus action, you can expend one superiority die and make a ranged attack with a weapon that has the thrown property. You can draw the weapon as part of making this attack. If you hit, add the superiority die to the weapon\\u0027s damage roll\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom6dab7084-000d-47e0-9012-27071a5e272e\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Quick Toss\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you make an Intelligence (Investigation), an Intelligence (History), or a Wisdom (Insight) check, you can expend one superiority die and add the superiority die to the ability check\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customdb6aba5a-1915-49f5-bb83-9ba9863f7d71\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Tactical Assessment\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1}],\"canReselect\":true,\"id\":\"292ed346-0ad7-4221-9752-4922b17b53af\",\"name\":\"Maneuvers\",\"selectedFeatures\":[]}],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[{\"abilityCalculators\":[],\"amountsPerLevel\":[{\"amount\":4,\"associatedValue\":\"d8\",\"level\":3},{\"amount\":5,\"associatedValue\":\"d8\",\"level\":7},{\"amount\":5,\"associatedValue\":\"d10\",\"level\":10},{\"amount\":6,\"associatedValue\":\"d10\",\"level\":15},{\"amount\":6,\"associatedValue\":\"d12\",\"level\":18}],\"associatedValueName\":\"Dice Type\",\"id\":\"2985a55b-8470-43ce-85f0-41d1578d5d8c\",\"name\":\"Superiority Dice\",\"type\":\"BASIC\",\"usesLeft\":0}],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[{\"hint\":\"\",\"level\":3,\"proficiency\":\"Choose 1 Artisan\\u0027s Tool\"}],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Whenever you hit with a weapon that you\\u0027re proficient with and deal damage, the weapon\\u0027s damage increases by 1d4\",\"level\":3},{\"description\":\"Whenever you hit with a weapon that you\\u0027re proficient with and deal damage, the weapon\\u0027s damage increases by 1d6\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"Whenever you hit with a weapon that you\\u0027re proficient with and deal damage, the weapon\\u0027s damage increases by 1d8\",\"level\":16},{\"description\":\"Whenever you hit with a weapon that you\\u0027re proficient with and deal damage, the weapon\\u0027s damage increases by 1d10\",\"level\":20}],\"id\":\"Custom611f73a9-fcfc-4d49-93dd-2bb0b8df06d7\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Brute Force\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Whenever you make a saving throw, roll 1d6 and add the die to your saving throw total. If applying this bonus to a death saving throw increases the total to 20 or higher, you gain the benefits of rolling a 20 on the d20\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Custom405c0fbf-7753-4329-8f4d-7b33d6c8c418\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Brutish Durability\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can choose a second option from the Fighting Style feature\",\"level\":10}],\"id\":\"Custom169321af-f553-4757-b089-7fdbb20cd111\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Additional Fighting Style\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":10},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you score a critical hit with a weapon attack, you gain a bonus to that weapon\\u0027s damage roll equal to your level in this class\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Custome2e4df2b-9026-44e3-99d7-fee56519b56a\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Devastating Critical\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"At the start of each of your turns in combat, you regain hit points equal to 5 + your Constitution modifier (minimum of 1 hit point). You don\\u0027t gain this benefit if you have 0 hit points or if you have more than half of your hit points left\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom7a334770-5983-4e86-8b1b-9900bc851927\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Survivor\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":18}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter_brute\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Brute\",\"selectableFeatures\":[{\"amountsPerLevel\":[{\"amount\":1,\"level\":10}],\"availableFeatures\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls you make with ranged weapons\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom8808a93c-1e6d-4a02-ba20-8f8a9f1383bc\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Archery\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"While you are wearing armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customfa2a0977-2fb7-42a1-b554-9a55bb1388eb\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Defense\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you are wielding a melee weapon in one hand and no other weapons, you gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls with that weapon\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom8875d140-b0f2-46ba-8fe2-897603efadae\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Dueling\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you roll a 1 or 2 on a damage die for an attack you make with a melee weapon that you are wielding with two hands, you can reroll the die and must use the new roll, even if the new roll is a 1 or a 2. The weapon must have the two-handed or versatile property for you to gain this benefit\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom19281b6d-3aeb-4657-97dc-dd36d2f2b00e\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Great Weapon Fighting\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When a creature you can see attacks a target other than you that is within 5 feet of you, you can use your reaction to impose disadvantage on the attack roll. You must be wielding a shield\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom1f90cee0-37f0-4781-9a64-0c762deeb71e\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Protection\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you engage in two-weapon fighting, you can add your ability modifier to the damage of the second attack\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom9cefba79-f725-462c-ac16-c2321adedab9\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Two-Weapon Fighting\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"As long as you are not wearing heavy armor or using a shield, you have a swimming speed and a climbing speed equal to your normal speed, and you gain a +1 bonus to AC\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customee6dabd5-46da-4c2b-ac66-e21e8971ec36\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Mariner\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You are trained in making ranged attack at close quarters. When making a ranged attack while you are within 5 feet of a hostile creature, you do not have disadvantage on the attack roll. Your ranged attacks ignore half cover and three-quarters cover against targets within 30 feet of you. Finally, you have a +1 bonus to attack rolls on ranged attacks\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom26611c38-020b-44eb-8ff9-03de56b6073a\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Close Quarters Shooter\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You excel at defending narrow passages, doorways, and other tight spaces. As a bonus action, you can enter a defensive stance that lasts until the start of your next turn. While in your defensive stance, you can make opportunity attacks without using your reaction, and you can use your reaction to make a melee attack against a creature that moves more than 5 feet while within your reach\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom69d3f2a0-3b58-4eb6-abad-ea8b1a2a6264\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Tunnel Fighter\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1}],\"canReselect\":false,\"id\":\"482d1370-a61f-4273-a892-bb532af44c60\",\"name\":\"Additional Fighting Style\",\"selectedFeatures\":[]}],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Animal Handling, History, Insight, Performance, or Persuasion. Alternatively, you learn one language of your choice\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom2ccb8cfc-e6b7-4e9a-bb01-b5b4e1c006ca\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Bonus Proficiencies\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You have advantage on saving throws made to avoid falling off your mount. If you fall off your mount and descend no more than 10 feet, you can land on your feet if you\\u0027re not incapacitated.\\n\\nFinally, mounting or dismounting a creature costs you only 5 feet of movement, rather than half your speed\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom0c12f975-f149-4600-83cf-a39be19bf5e9\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Born to the Saddle\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack, you can mark the creature until the end of your next turn. This effect ends early if you are incapacitated or you die, or if someone else marks the creature.\\n\\nWhile it is within 5 feet of you, a creature marked by you has disadvantage on any attack roll that doesn\\u0027t target you.\\n\\nIn addition, if a creature marked by you deals damage to anyone other than you, you can make a special melee weapon attack against the marked creature as a bonus action on your next turn. You have advantage on the attack roll, and if it hits, the attack\\u0027s weapon deals extra damage to the target equal to half your fighter level.\\n\\nRegardless of the number of creatures you mark, you can make this special attack a number of times equal to your Strength modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a long rest\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom7aa3f519-acde-45bf-935c-81d180bb728d\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Unwavering Mark\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"If you or a creature you can see within 5 feet of you is hit by an attack, you can roll 1d8 as a reaction if you\\u0027re wielding a melee weapon or a shield. Roll the die, and add the number rolled to the target\\u0027s AC against that attack. If the attack still hits, the target has resistance against the attack\\u0027s damage. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a long rest\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Customda1f3616-5271-44fa-ab6b-69d8ce08063b\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Warding Maneuver\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Creatures provoke an opportunity attack from you when they move 5 feet or more while within your reach, and if you hit a creature with an opportunity attack, the target\\u0027s speed is reduced to 0 until the end of the current turn\",\"level\":10}],\"id\":\"Customf2fd33cc-c076-425c-8c76-ec4b0aef5fcb\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Hold the Line\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":10},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"If you move at least 10 feet in a straight line right before attacking a creature and you hit it with the attack, that target must succeed on a Strength saving throw (DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier) or be knocked prone. You can use this feature only once on each of your turns\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Custom8477e7ec-4615-4ca8-bc93-26e39f398540\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Ferocious Charger\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"In combat, you get a special reaction that you can take once on every creature\\u0027s turn, except your turn. You can use this special reaction only to make an opportunity attack, and you can\\u0027t use it on the same turn that you take your normal reaction\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Customf4613271-caee-4227-81db-edb1ac61ba56\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Vigilant Defender\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":18}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter_cavalier\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Cavalier\",\"selectableFeatures\":[],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[{\"abilityCalculators\":[{\"calculators\":[{\"operands\":[{\"multiplierConstant\":1,\"operator\":\"PLUS\",\"stat\":\"STR\"}]},{\"operands\":[{\"multiplierConstant\":1,\"operator\":\"PLUS\"}]}],\"level\":3,\"topLevelConnector\":\"MAX\"}],\"amountsPerLevel\":[],\"associatedValueName\":\"\",\"id\":\"c0f0c215-8ba6-443e-96dd-56d2f404d9b0\",\"name\":\"Unwavering Mark Uses\",\"type\":\"ADVANCED\",\"usesLeft\":0},{\"abilityCalculators\":[{\"calculators\":[{\"operands\":[{\"multiplierConstant\":1,\"operator\":\"PLUS\",\"stat\":\"CON\"}]},{\"operands\":[{\"multiplierConstant\":1,\"operator\":\"PLUS\"}]}],\"level\":7,\"topLevelConnector\":\"MAX\"}],\"amountsPerLevel\":[],\"associatedValueName\":\"\",\"id\":\"9138ba9c-25e3-4454-90fa-6406e876dc28\",\"name\":\"Warding Maneuver Uses\",\"type\":\"ADVANCED\",\"usesLeft\":0}],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Your weapon attacks score a critical hit on a roll of 19 or 20\",\"level\":3},{\"description\":\"Your weapon attacks score a critical hit on a roll of 18-20\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Custom0d99c208-b92b-4993-a4fe-63de6cdb2fab\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Improved Critical\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can add half your proficiency bonus (round up) to any Strength, Dexterity or Constitution check you make that doesn\\u0027t already use your proficiency bonus. In addition, when you make a running long jump, the distance you can cover increases by a number of feet equal to your Strength modifier\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Custom03bcde2c-b013-4fab-9e6d-c955336bc338\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Remarkable Athlete\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can choose a second option from the Fighting Style class feature\",\"level\":10}],\"id\":\"Customd9a2d9ff-dfb5-4536-b4d5-d27c4273e360\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Additional Fighting Style\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":10},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Your weapon attacks score a critical hit on a roll of 18-20\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Custom4d7776e6-081c-4be5-ac5d-8fcbe0b0c7f3\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Superior Critical\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"At the start of each of your turns, you regain hit points equal to 5 + your constitution modifier if you have no more than half of your hit points left. You don\\u0027t gain this benefit if you have 0 hit points\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom32da06eb-390d-4320-a2fa-91b1bdaf867e\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Survivor\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":18}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter_champion\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Champion\",\"selectableFeatures\":[{\"amountsPerLevel\":[{\"amount\":1,\"level\":10}],\"availableFeatures\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls you make with ranged weapons\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom3a2161cb-bbb2-4f63-823e-b56b5636d17f\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Archery\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"While you are wearing armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom7dfd7a81-bd44-4485-8727-1d7c1a9745fc\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Defense\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you are wielding a melee weapon in one hand and no other weapons, you gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls with that weapon\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customd27d4030-e2a3-4789-864d-b880e887f3f9\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Dueling\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you roll a 1 or 2 on a damage die for an attack you make with a melee weapon that you are wielding with two hands, you can reroll the die and must use the new roll, even if the new roll is a 1 or a 2. The weapon must have the two-handed or versatile property for you to gain this benefit\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom237375e9-8d52-4eb4-8c28-6a0b87e13f2e\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Great Weapon Fighting\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When a creature you can see attacks a target other than you that is within 5 feet of you, you can use your reaction to impose disadvantage on the attack roll. You must be wielding a shield\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom74d6797e-d60a-4406-88e5-27b6405af4b3\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Protection\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you engage in two-weapon fighting, you can add your ability modifier to the damage of the second attack\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customf61927a7-2d80-4969-a052-83559c34f857\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Two-Weapon Fighting\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"As long as you are not wearing heavy armor or using a shield, you have a swimming speed and a climbing speed equal to your normal speed, and you gain a +1 bonus to AC\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom7d94ae9d-3aad-4d4a-8d43-6462f8dd337d\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Mariner\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You are trained in making ranged attack at close quarters. When making a ranged attack while you are within 5 feet of a hostile creature, you do not have disadvantage on the attack roll. Your ranged attacks ignore half cover and three-quarters cover against targets within 30 feet of you. Finally, you have a +1 bonus to attack rolls on ranged attacks\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom324b7e83-59d7-433b-809e-9f4eeaa6ab38\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Close Quarters Shooter\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You excel at defending narrow passages, doorways, and other tight spaces. As a bonus action, you can enter a defensive stance that lasts until the start of your next turn. While in your defensive stance, you can make opportunity attacks without using your reaction, and you can use your reaction to make a melee attack against a creature that moves more than 5 feet while within your reach\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom6812f88a-7592-459f-a35e-56c37b3941da\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Tunnel Fighter\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1}],\"canReselect\":false,\"id\":\"e86cd2cb-099a-41f0-85cc-5a3269028f53\",\"name\":\"Additional Fighting Style\",\"selectedFeatures\":[]}],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"THIRD\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You know with 2 cantrips and 3 spells from the wizard spell list. You have 2 1st level slots.\\n\\nSpell save DC \\u003d 8 + proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\\n\\nSpell attack mod \\u003d proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\",\"level\":3},{\"description\":\"You know with 2 cantrips and 4 spells from the wizard spell list. You have 3 1st level slots.\\n\\nSpell save DC \\u003d 8 + proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\\n\\nSpell attack mod \\u003d proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\",\"level\":4},{\"description\":\"You know with 2 cantrips and 5 spells from the wizard spell list. You have 4 1st level slots and 2 2nd level.\\n\\nSpell save DC \\u003d 8 + proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\\n\\nSpell attack mod \\u003d proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\",\"level\":7},{\"description\":\"You know with 2 cantrips and 6 spells from the wizard spell list. You have 4 1st level slots and 2 2nd level.\\n\\nSpell save DC \\u003d 8 + proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\\n\\nSpell attack mod \\u003d proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\",\"level\":8},{\"description\":\"You know with 3 cantrips and 7 spells from the wizard spell list. You have 4 1st level slots and 3 2nd level.\\n\\nSpell save DC \\u003d 8 + proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\\n\\nSpell attack mod \\u003d proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"You know with 3 cantrips and 8 spells from the wizard spell list. You have 4 1st level slots and 3 2nd level.\\n\\nSpell save DC \\u003d 8 + proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\\n\\nSpell attack mod \\u003d proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\",\"level\":11},{\"description\":\"You know with 3 cantrips and 9 spells from the wizard spell list. You have 4 1st level slots, 3 2nd level and 2 3rd level.\\n\\nSpell save DC \\u003d 8 + proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\\n\\nSpell attack mod \\u003d proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\",\"level\":13},{\"description\":\"You know with 3 cantrips and 10 spells from the wizard spell list. You have 4 1st level slots, 3 2nd level and 2 3rd level.\\n\\nSpell save DC \\u003d 8 + proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\\n\\nSpell attack mod \\u003d proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\",\"level\":14},{\"description\":\"You know with 3 cantrips and 11 spells from the wizard spell list. You have 4 1st level slots, 3 2nd level and 3 3rd level.\\n\\nSpell save DC \\u003d 8 + proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\\n\\nSpell attack mod \\u003d proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\",\"level\":16},{\"description\":\"You know with 3 cantrips and 12 spells from the wizard spell list. You have 4 1st level slots, 3 2nd level, 2 3rd level and 1 4th level.\\n\\nSpell save DC \\u003d 8 + proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\\n\\nSpell attack mod \\u003d proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\",\"level\":19},{\"description\":\"You know with 3 cantrips and 13 spells from the wizard spell list. You have 4 1st level slots, 3 2nd level, 2 3rd level and 1 4th level.\\n\\nSpell save DC \\u003d 8 + proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\\n\\nSpell attack mod \\u003d proficiency bonus + Intelligence mod\",\"level\":20}],\"id\":\"Custom1b70d988-91bc-42c5-9137-45176e666a0c\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Spellcasting\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Over the course of 1 hour short rest, you can bond a weapon to you. Once bonded, you cannot be disarmed unless you are incapacitated and if the weapon is on the same plane of existence, you can summon it to your hand as a bonus action. You can bond up to two weapons at once\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom7d9f0867-98a7-48b4-9cb9-4cee6f5ff3b2\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Weapon Bond\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can use your action to cast a cantrip and make one weapon attack as a bonus action\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Customcffa2abe-d2f2-4255-a8dc-2ece2bee28ea\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"War Magic\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Any creature you hit with a weapon attack has disadvantage on its next save it makes against a spell you cast before the end of your next turn\",\"level\":10}],\"id\":\"Customdd88b10a-5bb0-43a8-95b3-36b6d28935f0\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Eldritch Strike\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":10},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can teleport up to 30 feet to a space you can see when using your Action Surge. The teleport can take place before or after the Action Surge\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Custom2f03a8f6-02f4-4f03-b8fe-739578801bc4\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Arcane Charge\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can make one weapon attack as a bonus action whenever you use your action to cast a spell.\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Customaaf1a3a9-a21d-4aa6-830e-f00cc70b14bb\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Improved War Magic\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":18}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter_eldritch_knight\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Eldritch Knight\",\"selectableFeatures\":[],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain proficiency in two of the following skills of your choice: Arcana, History, Insight, Investigation, Nature, or Perception. You can gain proficiency with a tool of your choice in place of one skill choice\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom47b6f394-f5ef-4189-9bae-5a47f3cd9018\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Bonus Proficiencies\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain a set of abilities that are fueled by special dice called superiority dice. You have 4 superiority dice, which are d8s. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain all of your expended superiority dice when you finish a short or long rest. You can expend superiority dice to gain a number of different benefits:\\n\\n- When you make a weapon attack against a creature, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the attack roll. You can use this ability before or after making the attack roll, but before any of the effects of the attack are applied.\\n\\n- When you damage a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the damage roll. You can use this ability after rolling damage. If the attack causes the target to make a Constitution saving throw to maintain concentration, it has disadvantage on that save.\\n\\n- When you make an Intelligence, a Wisdom, or a Charisma saving throw, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the roll. You can use this feature only before you learn if the save succeeded or failed.\\n\\n- When you make a Wisdom (Perception) check to detect a hidden creature or object, or a Wisdom (Insight) check to determine if someone is lying to you, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the roll. You can use this feature after seeing the total but before learning if you succeeded or failed\",\"level\":3},{\"description\":\"You gain a set of abilities that are fueled by special dice called superiority dice. You have 5 superiority dice, which are d8s. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain all of your expended superiority dice when you finish a short or long rest. You can expend superiority dice to gain a number of different benefits:\\n\\n- When you make a weapon attack against a creature, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the attack roll. You can use this ability before or after making the attack roll, but before any of the effects of the attack are applied.\\n\\n- When you damage a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the damage roll. You can use this ability after rolling damage. If the attack causes the target to make a Constitution saving throw to maintain concentration, it has disadvantage on that save.\\n\\n- When you make an Intelligence, a Wisdom, or a Charisma saving throw, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the roll. You can use this feature only before you learn if the save succeeded or failed.\\n\\n- When you make a Wisdom (Perception) check to detect a hidden creature or object, or a Wisdom (Insight) check to determine if someone is lying to you, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the roll. You can use this feature after seeing the total but before learning if you succeeded or failed\",\"level\":7},{\"description\":\"You gain a set of abilities that are fueled by special dice called superiority dice. You have 5 superiority dice, which are d10s. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain all of your expended superiority dice when you finish a short or long rest. You can expend superiority dice to gain a number of different benefits:\\n\\n- When you make a weapon attack against a creature, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the attack roll. You can use this ability before or after making the attack roll, but before any of the effects of the attack are applied.\\n\\n- When you damage a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the damage roll. You can use this ability after rolling damage. If the attack causes the target to make a Constitution saving throw to maintain concentration, it has disadvantage on that save.\\n\\n- When you make an Intelligence, a Wisdom, or a Charisma saving throw, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the roll. You can use this feature only before you learn if the save succeeded or failed.\\n\\n- When you make a Wisdom (Perception) check to detect a hidden creature or object, or a Wisdom (Insight) check to determine if someone is lying to you, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the roll. You can use this feature after seeing the total but before learning if you succeeded or failed\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"You gain a set of abilities that are fueled by special dice called superiority dice. You have 6 superiority dice, which are d10s. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain all of your expended superiority dice when you finish a short or long rest. You can expend superiority dice to gain a number of different benefits:\\n\\n- When you make a weapon attack against a creature, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the attack roll. You can use this ability before or after making the attack roll, but before any of the effects of the attack are applied.\\n\\n- When you damage a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the damage roll. You can use this ability after rolling damage. If the attack causes the target to make a Constitution saving throw to maintain concentration, it has disadvantage on that save.\\n\\n- When you make an Intelligence, a Wisdom, or a Charisma saving throw, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the roll. You can use this feature only before you learn if the save succeeded or failed.\\n\\n- When you make a Wisdom (Perception) check to detect a hidden creature or object, or a Wisdom (Insight) check to determine if someone is lying to you, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the roll. You can use this feature after seeing the total but before learning if you succeeded or failed\",\"level\":15},{\"description\":\"You gain a set of abilities that are fueled by special dice called superiority dice. You have 6 superiority dice, which are d12s. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain all of your expended superiority dice when you finish a short or long rest. You can expend superiority dice to gain a number of different benefits:\\n\\n- When you make a weapon attack against a creature, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the attack roll. You can use this ability before or after making the attack roll, but before any of the effects of the attack are applied.\\n\\n- When you damage a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the damage roll. You can use this ability after rolling damage. If the attack causes the target to make a Constitution saving throw to maintain concentration, it has disadvantage on that save.\\n\\n- When you make an Intelligence, a Wisdom, or a Charisma saving throw, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the roll. You can use this feature only before you learn if the save succeeded or failed.\\n\\n- When you make a Wisdom (Perception) check to detect a hidden creature or object, or a Wisdom (Insight) check to determine if someone is lying to you, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the roll. You can use this feature after seeing the total but before learning if you succeeded or failed\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom465c58c7-d629-4e1e-9ed9-7e3db2bd3e08\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Combat Superiority\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can cast Detect Magic as a ritual. You can cast Protection from Evil and Good, but you cannot cast it again with this feature until you finish a long rest. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for these spells. In addition, you gain the ability to speak one of the following languages of your choice: Abyssal, Celestial, or Inferna\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom324aead2-e7ab-4ec8-95dd-90fc26709c2c\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Hunter\\u0027s Mysticism\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Whenever you expend superiority dice to add to a damage roll, you can expend up to two dice instead of just one, adding both to the roll. Both dice are expended as normal. If the target of your attack is an aberration, a fey, a fiend, or an undead, you deal maximum damage with both dice, instead of rolling them\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Custom61b23738-9be6-4592-98a3-0d46c5452630\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Monster Slayer\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Your superiority dice turn into d10s\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"Your superiority dice turn into d12s\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Customf37cd1dc-230f-4528-8cf1-9c5aeef7e0b6\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Imroved Combat Superiority\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":10},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you roll initiative and have no superiority dice remaining, you regain one superiority die\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Customa9ef6981-92c9-401d-bf71-9217bbee6fa2\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Relentless\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter_monster_hunter\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Monster Hunter\",\"selectableFeatures\":[],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[{\"abilityCalculators\":[],\"amountsPerLevel\":[{\"amount\":4,\"associatedValue\":\"d8\",\"level\":3},{\"amount\":5,\"associatedValue\":\"d8\",\"level\":7},{\"amount\":5,\"associatedValue\":\"d10\",\"level\":10},{\"amount\":6,\"associatedValue\":\"d10\",\"level\":15},{\"amount\":6,\"associatedValue\":\"d12\",\"level\":18}],\"associatedValueName\":\"Dice Type\",\"id\":\"4196c575-5e51-4613-956e-f6decf20d36a\",\"name\":\"Superiority Dice\",\"type\":\"BASIC\",\"usesLeft\":0}],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"artificer__eb_, artificer__revised_, bard, cleric, druid, paladin, ranger__revised__, revised_ranger, ranger, sorcerer, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, S\",\"description\":\"For the duration, you sense the presence of magic within 30 feet of you. If you sense magic in this way, you can use your action to see a faint aura around any visible creature or object in the area that bears magic, and you learn its school of magic, if any.\\n\\nThe spell can penetrate most barriers, but it is blocked by 1 foot of stone, 1 inch of common metal, a thin sheet of lead, or 3 feet of wood or dirt.\",\"duration\":\"Concentration, up to 10 minutes\",\"higherLevels\":\"\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":true,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Detect Magic\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"Self\",\"school\":\"divination\",\"type\":\"1st-level divination (Ritual)\"}},{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"cleric, paladin, warlock, blood_hunter, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, S, M (holy water or powdered silver and iron, which the spell consumes)\",\"description\":\"Until the spell ends, one willing creature you touch is protected against certain types of creatures: aberrations, celestials, elementals, fey, fiends, and undead.\\nThe protection grants several benefits. Creatures of those types have disadvantage on attack rolls against the target. The target also can\\u0027t be charmed, frightened, or possessed by them. If the target is already charmed, frightened, or possessed by such a creature, the target has advantage on any new saving throw against the relevant effect.\",\"duration\":\"Concentration, up to 10 minutes\",\"higherLevels\":\"\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Protection from Evil and Good\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"Touch\",\"school\":\"abjuration\",\"type\":\"1st-level abjuration\"}}],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Purple Dragon knights are tied to a specific order of Cormyrean knighthood. Banneret serves as the generic name for this archetype if you use it in other campaign settings or to model warlords other than Purple Dragon knights\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom0c975c78-5616-4c98-b102-73abbecd7ba6\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Restriction: Knighthood\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you use your Second Wind feature, you can choose up to three creatures within 60 feet of you that are allied with you. Each one regains hit points equal to your fighter level, provided that the creature can see or hear you\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom1abfb59e-f48e-47fc-a129-a499bb4d2fed\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Rallying Cry\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain proficiency in the Persuasion skill. If you are already proficient in it, you gain proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Animal Handling, Insight, Intimidation, or Performance. Your proficiency bonus is doubled for any ability check you make that uses Persuasion. You receive this benefit regardless of the skill proficiency you gain from this feature\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Custom6bfc065c-6fa6-41a2-af84-400b4cc494e3\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Royal Envoy\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you use your Action Surge feature, you can choose one creature within 60 feet of you that is allied with you. That creature can make one melee or ranged weapon attack with its reaction, provided that it can see or hear you\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"When you use your Action Surge feature, you can choose two creatures within 60 feet of you that is allied with you. That creature can make one melee or ranged weapon attack with its reaction, provided that it can see or hear you\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Customc36a4898-1fad-44d1-9550-a3737e831940\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Inspiring Surge\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":10},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you decide to use Indomitable to reroll an Intelligence, a Wisdom, or a Charisma saving throw and you aren\\u0027t incapacitated, you can choose one ally within 60 feet of you that also failed its saving throw against the same effect. If that creature can see or hear you, it can reroll its saving throw and must use the new roll\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Custom2f0a60f4-3843-4d6c-8436-fd27a4964ec0\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Bulwark\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter_purple_dragon_knight\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Purple Dragon Knight\",\"selectableFeatures\":[],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[{\"hint\":\"\",\"level\":7,\"proficiency\":\"full,persuasion\"}],\"specialAbilities\":[],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: History, Insight, Performance, or Persuasion. Alternatively, you learn one language of your choice\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom14d70f74-1d60-46a8-9158-e07fd208ad5d\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Bonus Proficiency\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"As a bonus action on your turn, you can give yourself advantage on weapon attack rolls until the end of the current turn. When you do so, you also gain 5 temporary hit points. You can use this feature three times, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a long rest\",\"level\":3},{\"description\":\"As a bonus action on your turn, you can give yourself advantage on weapon attack rolls until the end of the current turn. When you do so, you also gain 10 temporary hit points. You can use this feature three times, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a long rest\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"As a bonus action on your turn, you can give yourself advantage on weapon attack rolls until the end of the current turn. When you do so, you also gain 15 temporary hit points. You can use this feature three times, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a long rest\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Custom7ccdd4d1-ffc5-46ff-839a-85a9f3c2124c\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Fighting Spirit\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Whenever you make a Charisma (Persuasion) check, you gain a bonus to the check equal to your Wisdom modifier. You also gain proficiency in Wisdom saving throws. If you already have this proficiency, you instead gain proficiency in Intelligence or Charisma saving throws (your choice)\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Custome31bf8fc-a4cf-4ac1-9029-dbd869aabe68\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Elegant Courtier\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you roll initiative and have no uses of Fighting Spirit remaining, you regain one use\",\"level\":10}],\"id\":\"Customdbc99fe4-6d93-4f99-a09b-6a06683c218c\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Tireless Spirit\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":10},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"If you take the Attack action on your turn and have advantage on an attack roll against one of the targets, you can forgo the advantage for that roll to make an additional weapon attack against that target, as part of the same action. You can only do so once per turn\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Customa4e35579-0737-4145-ad14-5d8a7a8a304b\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Rapid Strike\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"If you take damage that reduces you to 0 hit points and doesn\\u0027t kill you outright, you can use your reaction to delay falling unconscious and immediately take an extra turn. While you have 0 hit points during that extra turn, taking damage causes death saving throw failures as normal, and three death saving throw failures can still kill you. When the extra turn ends, you fall unconscious if you still have 0 hit points. Once you use this feature, you can\\u0027t use it again until you finish a long rest\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Customfea05010-fe43-4541-984a-099c7d813482\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Strength Before Death\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":18}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter_samurai\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Samurai\",\"selectableFeatures\":[],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[{\"abilityCalculators\":[],\"amountsPerLevel\":[{\"amount\":3,\"associatedValue\":\"5\",\"level\":3},{\"amount\":3,\"associatedValue\":\"10\",\"level\":10},{\"amount\":3,\"associatedValue\":\"15\",\"level\":15}],\"associatedValueName\":\"Temp HP\",\"id\":\"fe79088c-1dc9-478c-bd7c-a5321713f6f0\",\"name\":\"Fighting Spirit Uses\",\"type\":\"BASIC\",\"usesLeft\":0}],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain proficiency in three of the following skills of your choice: Acrobatics, Athletics, Investigation, Medicine, Nature, Perception, Stealth, or Survival. You can choose to gain proficiency with thieves\\u0027 tools in place of one skill choice\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom86fede58-1c11-4c34-808e-1229679ff64a\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Bonus Proficiencies\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You have 4 superiority dice, which are d8s. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain all of your expended superiority dice when you finish a long or short rest. You can expend superiority dice to gain a number of different benefits:\\n\\n- When you make a check that allows you to apply your proficiency in Athletics, Nature, Perception, Stealth, or Survival, you can expend one superiority die to bolster the check. Add half the number rolled on the superiority die (rounding up) to your check. You apply this bonus after making the check but before learning if it was successful.\\n\\n- When you make a weapon attack against a creature, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the attack roll. You can use this ability before or after making the attack roll, but before any of the effects of the attack are applied.\\n\\n- If you are hit by an attack while wearing light or medium armor, you can expend one superiority die as a reaction, adding the number rolled to your AC. If the attack still hits, you take half damage from it\",\"level\":3},{\"description\":\"You have 5 superiority dice, which are d8s. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain all of your expended superiority dice when you finish a long or short rest. You can expend superiority dice to gain a number of different benefits:\\n\\n- When you make a check that allows you to apply your proficiency in Athletics, Nature, Perception, Stealth, or Survival, you can expend one superiority die to bolster the check. Add half the number rolled on the superiority die (rounding up) to your check. You apply this bonus after making the check but before learning if it was successful.\\n\\n- When you make a weapon attack against a creature, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the attack roll. You can use this ability before or after making the attack roll, but before any of the effects of the attack are applied.\\n\\n- If you are hit by an attack while wearing light or medium armor, you can expend one superiority die as a reaction, adding the number rolled to your AC. If the attack still hits, you take half damage from it\",\"level\":7},{\"description\":\"You have 5 superiority dice, which are d10s. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain all of your expended superiority dice when you finish a long or short rest. You can expend superiority dice to gain a number of different benefits:\\n\\n- When you make a check that allows you to apply your proficiency in Athletics, Nature, Perception, Stealth, or Survival, you can expend one superiority die to bolster the check. Add half the number rolled on the superiority die (rounding up) to your check. You apply this bonus after making the check but before learning if it was successful.\\n\\n- When you make a weapon attack against a creature, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the attack roll. You can use this ability before or after making the attack roll, but before any of the effects of the attack are applied.\\n\\n- If you are hit by an attack while wearing light or medium armor, you can expend one superiority die as a reaction, adding the number rolled to your AC. If the attack still hits, you take half damage from it\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"You have 6 superiority dice, which are d10s. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain all of your expended superiority dice when you finish a long or short rest. You can expend superiority dice to gain a number of different benefits:\\n\\n- When you make a check that allows you to apply your proficiency in Athletics, Nature, Perception, Stealth, or Survival, you can expend one superiority die to bolster the check. Add half the number rolled on the superiority die (rounding up) to your check. You apply this bonus after making the check but before learning if it was successful.\\n\\n- When you make a weapon attack against a creature, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the attack roll. You can use this ability before or after making the attack roll, but before any of the effects of the attack are applied.\\n\\n- If you are hit by an attack while wearing light or medium armor, you can expend one superiority die as a reaction, adding the number rolled to your AC. If the attack still hits, you take half damage from it\",\"level\":15},{\"description\":\"You have 6 superiority dice, which are d12s. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain all of your expended superiority dice when you finish a long or short rest. You can expend superiority dice to gain a number of different benefits:\\n\\n- When you make a check that allows you to apply your proficiency in Athletics, Nature, Perception, Stealth, or Survival, you can expend one superiority die to bolster the check. Add half the number rolled on the superiority die (rounding up) to your check. You apply this bonus after making the check but before learning if it was successful.\\n\\n- When you make a weapon attack against a creature, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the attack roll. You can use this ability before or after making the attack roll, but before any of the effects of the attack are applied.\\n\\n- If you are hit by an attack while wearing light or medium armor, you can expend one superiority die as a reaction, adding the number rolled to your AC. If the attack still hits, you take half damage from it\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom8b38939e-e8af-4d04-89dd-5d5a5828e73e\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Combat Superiority\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Choose one type of favored terrain: arctic, coast, desert, forest, grassland, mountain, swamp, or the Underdark. When you make an Intelligence or Wisdom check related to your favored terrain, your proficiency bonus is doubled if you are using a skill that you’re proficient in.\\n\\nWhile traveling for an hour or more in your favored terrain, you gain the following benefits:\\n\\n- Difficult terrain doesn’t slow your group’s travel.\\n- Your group can’t become lost except by magical means.\\n- Even when you are engaged in another activity while traveling (such as foraging, navigating, or tracking), you remain alert to danger.\\n- If you are traveling alone, you can move stealthily at a normal pace.\\n- When you forage, you find twice as much food as you normally would.\\n- While tracking other creatures, you also learn their exact number, their sizes, and how long ago they passed through the area.\\n\\nYou choose additional favored terrain types at 7th and 15th level\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom8f9552eb-2505-4d37-be58-4c727801c7b4\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Natural Explorer\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Your superiority dice turn into d10s\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"Your superiority dice turn into d12s\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom60ca4247-87c8-4b45-ac00-98c2c9f49266\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Improved Combat Superiority\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":10},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You roll initiative and have no superiority dice remaining, you regain 1 superiority die\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Custom423c52c1-4494-4e04-a7bf-d2145cc14e26\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Relentless\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter_scout\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Scout\",\"selectableFeatures\":[{\"amountsPerLevel\":[{\"amount\":1,\"level\":3},{\"amount\":2,\"level\":7},{\"amount\":3,\"level\":15}],\"availableFeatures\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain the \\u0027Natural Explorer\\u0027 feature effects for this terrain\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom47c54fbd-df63-4463-9fef-4341a0c1d4fb\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Arctic\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain the \\u0027Natural Explorer\\u0027 feature effects for this terrain\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customde71e81e-0fef-4c27-a210-795242f943e6\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Coast\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain the \\u0027Natural Explorer\\u0027 feature effects for this terrain\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom2d4514d7-d78b-44e6-a720-417cc31858a9\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Desert\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain the \\u0027Natural Explorer\\u0027 feature effects for this terrain\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom78b812f8-5d58-4201-96fa-2a37adcd16ad\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Forest\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain the \\u0027Natural Explorer\\u0027 feature effects for this terrain\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom3fab5d48-8b8c-4a60-9695-47065d700bf7\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Grassland\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain the \\u0027Natural Explorer\\u0027 feature effects for this terrain\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customefaab845-4405-4b8a-b33c-0b58bf62d8cc\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Mountain\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain the \\u0027Natural Explorer\\u0027 feature effects for this terrain\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom148aa0c5-ccaa-472b-a5ac-ae9d9db5df1f\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Swamp\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain the \\u0027Natural Explorer\\u0027 feature effects for this terrain\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom9cce8c9e-536a-4d8f-94a4-63c50b04dd02\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Underdark\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1}],\"canReselect\":false,\"id\":\"c82022d2-40ba-439a-9efc-8129a50ae248\",\"name\":\"Favored Terrains\",\"selectedFeatures\":[]}],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[{\"abilityCalculators\":[],\"amountsPerLevel\":[{\"amount\":4,\"associatedValue\":\"d8\",\"level\":3},{\"amount\":5,\"associatedValue\":\"d8\",\"level\":7},{\"amount\":5,\"associatedValue\":\"d10\",\"level\":10},{\"amount\":6,\"associatedValue\":\"d10\",\"level\":15},{\"amount\":6,\"associatedValue\":\"d12\",\"level\":18}],\"associatedValueName\":\"Dice Type\",\"id\":\"2ce872da-0265-4ab8-b0a9-e7e929735f6e\",\"name\":\"Superiority Dice\",\"type\":\"BASIC\",\"usesLeft\":0}],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Your aim becomes deadly. As a bonus action on your turn, you can take careful aim at a creature you can see that is within range of a ranged weapon you\\u0027re wielding. Until the end of this turn, your ranged attacks with that weapon gain two benefits against the target:\\n\\n- The attacks ignore half and three-quarters cover.\\n- On each hit, the weapon deals additional damage to the target equal to 2 + half your fighter level.\\n\\nYou can use this feature three times. You regain all expended uses of it when you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom02a86fdf-aef6-4cd3-ab40-ec07c0dd148e\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Steady Aim\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can take the Search action as a bonus action. You also gain proficiency in the Perception, Investigation, or Survival skill (choose one)\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Custom47391c7b-13ec-428d-8c62-9cdf753f2ab6\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Careful Eyes\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Making a ranged attack roll while within 5 feet of an enemy doesn\\u0027t impose disadvantage on your roll. In addition, if you hit a creature within 5 feet of you with a ranged attack on your turn, that creature can\\u0027t take reactions until the end of this turn\",\"level\":10}],\"id\":\"Custom586c20ba-b5d3-4bef-a2a4-31a2b7fc3224\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Close-Quarters Shooting\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":10},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"If you have advantage on a weapon attack against a target on your turn, you can forgo that advantage to immediately make an additional weapon attack against the same target as a bonus action\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Custom8ea1beec-71b1-4061-bb67-09bcacf71c0a\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Rapid Strike\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"If you take the Attack action on your first turn of a combat, you can make one additional ranged weapon attack as part of that action\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom35a88995-1af2-49a7-bef0-40dbd0eb71b6\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Snap Shot\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":18}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter_sharpshooter\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Sharpshooter\",\"selectableFeatures\":[],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[{\"abilityCalculators\":[],\"amountsPerLevel\":[{\"amount\":3,\"level\":3}],\"associatedValueName\":\"\",\"id\":\"1dda0f5a-d972-4c17-af71-5563f25bc70e\",\"name\":\"Steady Aim Uses\",\"type\":\"BASIC\",\"usesLeft\":0}],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain proficiency with firearms, allowing you to add your proficiency bonus to attacks made with firearms\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom026ccc82-91fe-456a-957b-5959993329c4\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Firearm Proficiency\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain proficiency with Tinker’s Tools. You may use them to craft ammunition at half the cost, repair damaged firearms, or even draft and create new ones (DM’s discretion). Some extremely experimental and intricate firearms are only available through crafting.\\n\\nFirearm Properties:\\nFirearms are a new and volatile technology, and as such bring their own unique set of weapon properties. Some properties are followed by a number, and this number signifies an element of that property (outlined below). These properties replace the optional ones. Firearms are ranged weapons.\\n\\n- Reload: The weapon can be fired a number of times equal to its Reload score before you must spend 1 attack or 1 action to reload. You must have one free hand to reload a firearm.\\n\\n- Misfire: Whenever you make an attack roll with a firearm, and the dice roll is equal to or lower than the weapon’s Misfire score, the weapon misfires. The attack misses, and the weapon cannot be used again until you spend an action to try and repair it. To repair your firearm, you must make a successful Tinker’s Tools check (DC equal to 8 + misfire score). If your check fails, the weapon is broken and must be mended out of combat at a quarter of the cost of the firearm. Creatures who use a firearm without being proficient increase the weapon’s misfire score by 1.\\n\\n- Explosive: Upon a hit, everything within 5 ft of the target must make a Dexterity saving throw (DC equal to 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier) or suffer 1d8 fire damage. If the weapon misses, the ammunition fails to detonate, or bounces away harmlessly before doing so.\\n\\nAmmunition:\\nAll firearms require ammunition to make an attack, and due to their rare nature, ammunition may be near impossible to find or purchase. However, if materials are gathered, you can craft ammunition yourself using your Tinker’s Tools at half the cost. Each firearm uses its own unique ammunition and is generally sold or crafted in batches listed below next to the price\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom312751b7-0b58-4eca-95c8-ea12f8e5b049\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Gunsmith\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You learn to perform powerful trick shots to disable or damage your opponents using your firearms. You know two trick shots of your choice. Each time you learn a new trick shot, you can also replace one trick shot you know with a different one.\\n\\nMany maneuvers enhance an attack in some way. Each use of a trick shot must be declared before the attack roll is made. You can use only one trick shot per attack.\\n\\nGrit: You gain a number of grit points equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of 1). You regain 1 expended grit point each time you roll a 20 on the d20 roll for an attack with a firearm, or deal a killing blow with a firearm to a creature of significant threat (DM’s discretion). You regain all expended grit points after a short or long rest.\\n\\nSaving Throws:\\nSome of your trick shots require your targets to make a saving throw to resist the trick shot’s effects. The saving throw DC is calculated as follows:\\n\\nTrick Shot save DC \\u003d 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier\",\"level\":3},{\"description\":\"You learn to perform powerful trick shots to disable or damage your opponents using your firearms. You know three trick shots of your choice. Each time you learn a new trick shot, you can also replace one trick shot you know with a different one.\\n\\nMany maneuvers enhance an attack in some way. Each use of a trick shot must be declared before the attack roll is made. You can use only one trick shot per attack.\\n\\nGrit: You gain a number of grit points equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of 1). You regain 1 expended grit point each time you roll a 20 on the d20 roll for an attack with a firearm, or deal a killing blow with a firearm to a creature of significant threat (DM’s discretion). You regain all expended grit points after a short or long rest.\\n\\nSaving Throws:\\nSome of your trick shots require your targets to make a saving throw to resist the trick shot’s effects. The saving throw DC is calculated as follows:\\n\\nTrick Shot save DC \\u003d 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier\",\"level\":7},{\"description\":\"You learn to perform powerful trick shots to disable or damage your opponents using your firearms. You know four trick shots of your choice. Each time you learn a new trick shot, you can also replace one trick shot you know with a different one.\\n\\nMany maneuvers enhance an attack in some way. Each use of a trick shot must be declared before the attack roll is made. You can use only one trick shot per attack.\\n\\nGrit: You gain a number of grit points equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of 1). You regain 1 expended grit point each time you roll a 20 on the d20 roll for an attack with a firearm, or deal a killing blow with a firearm to a creature of significant threat (DM’s discretion). You regain all expended grit points after a short or long rest.\\n\\nSaving Throws:\\nSome of your trick shots require your targets to make a saving throw to resist the trick shot’s effects. The saving throw DC is calculated as follows:\\n\\nTrick Shot save DC \\u003d 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"You learn to perform powerful trick shots to disable or damage your opponents using your firearms. You know five trick shots of your choice. Each time you learn a new trick shot, you can also replace one trick shot you know with a different one.\\n\\nMany maneuvers enhance an attack in some way. Each use of a trick shot must be declared before the attack roll is made. You can use only one trick shot per attack.\\n\\nGrit: You gain a number of grit points equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of 1). You regain 1 expended grit point each time you roll a 20 on the d20 roll for an attack with a firearm, or deal a killing blow with a firearm to a creature of significant threat (DM’s discretion). You regain all expended grit points after a short or long rest.\\n\\nSaving Throws:\\nSome of your trick shots require your targets to make a saving throw to resist the trick shot’s effects. The saving throw DC is calculated as follows:\\n\\nTrick Shot save DC \\u003d 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier\",\"level\":15},{\"description\":\"You learn to perform powerful trick shots to disable or damage your opponents using your firearms. You know six trick shots of your choice. Each time you learn a new trick shot, you can also replace one trick shot you know with a different one.\\n\\nMany maneuvers enhance an attack in some way. Each use of a trick shot must be declared before the attack roll is made. You can use only one trick shot per attack.\\n\\nGrit: You gain a number of grit points equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of 1). You regain 1 expended grit point each time you roll a 20 on the d20 roll for an attack with a firearm, or deal a killing blow with a firearm to a creature of significant threat (DM’s discretion). You regain all expended grit points after a short or long rest.\\n\\nSaving Throws:\\nSome of your trick shots require your targets to make a saving throw to resist the trick shot’s effects. The saving throw DC is calculated as follows:\\n\\nTrick Shot save DC \\u003d 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Customd119ad8b-6ccf-4b80-a044-a68e2da035f6\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Adept Marksman\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You add your proficiency bonus to your initiative. You can also stow a firearm, then draw another firearm as a single object interaction on your turn\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Custom3810ff90-2c0a-4e94-b5f9-db3b727fb601\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Quickdraw\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You learn how to quickly attempt to fix a jammed gun. You can spend a grit point to attempt to repair a misfired (but not broken) firearm as a bonus action\",\"level\":10}],\"id\":\"Customc14ffcd7-8b55-41af-8fe0-a6fbbc761f0c\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Rapid Repair\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":10},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can reload any firearm as a bonus action\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Custom31a62ad8-9e37-4de5-a6d1-c1e9be5e31fe\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Lightning Reload\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Your firearm attacks score a critical hit on a roll of 19-20, and you regain a grit point on a roll of 19 or 20 on a d20 attack roll\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Customd0c5bd0c-392d-476c-8b28-eb414ffc79e0\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Vicious Intent\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":18},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Whenever you score a critical hit on an attack with a firearm, the target additionally suffers half of the damage from the attack at the end of its next turn\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom6bdbdcbb-8b74-4130-9f43-c11b61d6f921\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Hemorrhaging Critical\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":18}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter_gunslinger\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Gunslinger\",\"selectableFeatures\":[{\"amountsPerLevel\":[{\"amount\":2,\"level\":3},{\"amount\":3,\"level\":7},{\"amount\":4,\"level\":10},{\"amount\":5,\"level\":15},{\"amount\":6,\"level\":18}],\"availableFeatures\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can use the powerful blast and thundering sound of your firearm to shake the resolve of a creature. You can expend one grit point while making a Charisma (Intimidation) check to gain advantage on the roll\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom8c1b0974-882e-43ac-a7ca-e7c975ba64b0\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Bullying Shot\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you make a firearm attack against a creature, you can expend one grit point to attempt to dizzy your opponent. On a hit, the creature suffers normal damage and must make a Constitution saving throw or suffer disadvantage on attacks until the end of their next turn\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom5dc144e3-948c-49d0-8269-4ee3aeb2920a\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Dazing Shot\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you make a firearm attack against a creature, you can expend one grit point to gain advantage on the attack roll\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Customebe78303-ecc8-41e0-a04f-13236c3099f2\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Deadeye Shot\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you make a firearm attack against a creature, you can expend one grit point to attempt to shoot an object from their hands. On a hit, the creature suffers normal damage and must succeed on a Strength saving throw or drop 1 held object of your choice and have that object be pushed 10 feet away from you\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom5b4a63b5-e8a6-4741-99a8-dd46c2932c25\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Disarming Shot\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you make a firearm attack against a creature, you can expend one grit point to attempt to trip them up and force them back. On a hit, the creature suffers normal damage and must succeed on a Strength saving throw or be pushed 15 feet away from you\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom020b7e9c-e5d7-4195-a04d-f80fdfe70e56\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Forceful Shot\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you make a firearm attack against a creature, you can expend one grit point to attempt to fire through multiple opponents. The initial attack gains a +1 to the firearm’s misfire score. On a hit, the creature suffers normal damage and you make an attack roll with disadvantage against every creature in a line directly behind the target within your first range increment. Only the initial attack can misfire\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom578198ba-fad4-4655-bd82-bc366042c229\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Piercing Shot\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you make a firearm attack against a creature, you can expend one or more grit points to enhance the volatility of the attack. For each grit point expended, the attack gains a +2 to the firearm’s misfire score. If the attack hits, you can roll one additional weapon damage die per grit point spent when determining the damage\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Customb9e0f0d3-1991-4787-89e2-31a9daffebbb\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Violent Shot\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"When you make a firearm attack against a creature, you can expend one grit point to attempt to topple a moving target. On a hit, the creature suffers normal damage and must make a Strength saving throw or be knocked prone\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom39f19817-99a5-4883-b467-ccb3a89cccbc\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Winging Shot\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3}],\"canReselect\":true,\"id\":\"b2d57d23-c5a1-410f-be6d-30f61ae6bb53\",\"name\":\"Trick Shots\",\"selectedFeatures\":[]}],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[],\"weaponProficiencies\":[{\"hint\":\"\",\"level\":3,\"proficiency\":\"Firearm\"}]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain proficiency with smith’s tools, and you learn to speak, read, and write Giant\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custombdff6b63-8d4b-441f-833a-0a136b4c266c\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Bonus Proficiencies\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You learn how to use runes to enhance your gear. When you gain this feature, you learn how to inscribe two runes of your choice on weapons, armor, or shields (see each rune for details).\\n\\nWhenever you finish a long rest, you can touch a number of objects equal to the number of runes you know, and you inscribe a different rune onto each of the objects. To be eligible, an object must be a weapon, a suit of armor, or a shield.\\n\\nYour rune remains on an object until you finish a long rest, and an object can bear only one of your runes.\\n\\nEach time you gain a level in this class, you can replace one rune you know with a different one.\\n\\nRunes always provide magical effects.\\n\\nIf a rune requires a saving throw, your Rune Magic save DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Intelligence modifier\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom9fd2a39a-d2eb-4350-8d75-bdc1d0271f5d\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Rune Magic\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can imbue yourself with the might of giants. As a bonus action, you magically gain the following benefits, which last for 1 minute:\\n\\n- If you are smaller than Large, you become Large, along with anything you are wearing. If you lack the room to become Large, your size doesn’t change.\\n\\n- You have advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws.\\n\\n- Your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d6 damage.\\n\\nYou can use this feature twice, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a long rest\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Customca9c5f5e-66d1-45be-8d21-96696ace20ce\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Giant Might\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You learn to invoke your rune magic to protect your allies. When another creature you can see within 60 feet of you is hit by an attack roll, you can use your reaction to grant a bonus to the creature’s AC against that attack. The bonus equals 1 + your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +2).\\n\\nIn addition, you learn one new rune of your choice from the Rune Magic feature (for a total of three)\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Custom2aefc5c0-4bde-4546-8d0c-da84501930cc\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Defensive Runes\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"The magic of your runes permanently alters you. When you gain this feature, roll 3d4. You grow a number of inches in height equal to the roll. Moreover, the extra damage you deal with your Giant Might feature increases to 1d8.\\n\\nIn addition, you learn one new rune of your choice from your Rune Magic feature (for a total of four)\",\"level\":10}],\"id\":\"Custom14db9296-9510-48a7-9194-9828548f25f8\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Great Stature\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":10},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can invoke each rune you know from your Rune Magic feature twice, rather than once, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a short or long rest.\\n\\nIn addition, you learn one new rune of your choice from the Rune Magic feature (for a total of five)\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Custom07972b5c-b711-4755-90b7-a5d52b88f002\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Rune Magic Mastery\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You learn how to share your rune magic with your allies. When you use your Giant Might feature, you can choose one willing creature you can see within 60 feet of you. The chosen creature also gains the benefits of your Giant Might feature\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Customd162dff3-b59f-49fe-9283-15d882ef9d0c\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Blessing of the All Father\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":18}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter_rune_knight_[ua]\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[{\"hint\":\"\",\"level\":3,\"proficiency\":\"Giant\"}],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Rune Knight [UA]\",\"selectableFeatures\":[{\"amountsPerLevel\":[{\"amount\":2,\"level\":3},{\"amount\":2,\"level\":4},{\"amount\":2,\"level\":5},{\"amount\":2,\"level\":6},{\"amount\":3,\"level\":7},{\"amount\":3,\"level\":8},{\"amount\":3,\"level\":9},{\"amount\":4,\"level\":10},{\"amount\":4,\"level\":11},{\"amount\":4,\"level\":12},{\"amount\":4,\"level\":13},{\"amount\":4,\"level\":14},{\"amount\":5,\"level\":15},{\"amount\":5,\"level\":16},{\"amount\":5,\"level\":17},{\"amount\":5,\"level\":18},{\"amount\":5,\"level\":19},{\"amount\":5,\"level\":20}],\"availableFeatures\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"This rune’s magic bestows a resilience reminiscent of a hill giant. While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, you have advantage on saving throws against being poisoned, and you have resistance against poison damage.\\n\\nIn addition, you can invoke the rune as a bonus action, gaining resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage for 1 minute. Once you invoke the rune, you can’t do so again until you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom182fc53c-d612-4039-a79c-ea63e908b0fc\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Haug (Hill Rune)\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"This rune’s magic channels the masterful craftsmanship of fire giant smiths. While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, your proficiency bonus is doubled for any ability check you make that uses your proficiency with a tool.\\n\\nIn addition, when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can invoke the rune to summon fiery shackles: the target must succeed on a Strength saving throw or be restrained for 1 minute. While restrained by the shackles, the target takes 2d6 fire damage at the start of each of its turns. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, banishing the shackles on a success. Once you invoke the rune, you can’t do so again until you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Customb98cb15f-8caa-482b-9c21-a996326f5983\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Ild (Fire Rune)\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"This rune’s magic evokes a frost giant’s stoic calm. While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, you have advantage on Wisdom (Animal Handling) checks and Charisma (Intimidation) checks.\\n\\nIn addition, you can invoke the rune as a bonus action to increase your Strength score by 2 for 10 minutes. This increase can cause your score to exceed 20, but not 30. Once you invoke the rune, you can’t do so again until you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom6b54d4fb-ce4d-49e7-9616-2cf8056520f7\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Ise (Frost Rune)\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"This rune’s magic emulates the deceptiveness of a cloud giant. While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, you have advantage on Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) checks and Charisma (Deception) checks.\\n\\nIn addition, when you or a creature you can see within 30 feet of you is hit by an attack roll, you can use your reaction to invoke the rune and cause that attack to target a different creature within 30 feet of you (other than the attacker), using the same roll. This magic can transfer the attack regardless of the attack’s range. Once you invoke the rune, you can’t do so again until you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Customa709022e-e6f7-4b49-be49-37bbc8bdcd39\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Skye (Cloud Rune)\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"This rune’s magic channels the insightfulness of a stone giant. While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, you have advantage on Wisdom (Insight) checks, and you have darkvision out to a range of 60 feet. If you already have darkvision, its range increases by 30 feet.\\n\\nIn addition, when a creature you can see ends its turn within 30 feet of you, you can use your reaction to invoke the rune and force the creature to make a Wisdom saving throw. Unless the save succeeds, the creature is charmed by you for 1 minute. While charmed in this way, the creature has a speed of 0 and is incapacitated, descending into a dreamy stupor. The effect ends if the charmed creature takes any damage or if someone else uses an action to shake the creature out of its haze. Once you invoke the rune, you can’t do so again until you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Customaff3cee0-9130-4485-b131-76ccbb36b805\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Stein (Stone Rune)\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Using this rune, you can glimpse the future like a storm giant. While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, you have advantage on Intelligence (Arcana) checks, and you can’t be surprised as long as you are not incapacitated.\\n\\nIn addition, you can invoke the rune as a bonus action to enter a prophetic state for 1 minute or until you’re incapacitated. Until the state ends, when you or another creature you can see within 60 feet of you makes an attack roll, a saving throw, or an ability check, you can use your reaction to cause the roll to have advantage or disadvantage. Once you invoke the rune, you can’t do so again until you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Customad20315f-c23c-4e84-be80-34c01666dc15\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Uvar (Storm Rune)\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3}],\"canReselect\":true,\"id\":\"0f736944-9791-48b9-a8b1-7716cdf421dc\",\"name\":\"Runes Known\",\"selectedFeatures\":[]}],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[{\"hint\":\"\",\"level\":3,\"proficiency\":\"Smith\\u0027s tools\"}],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can use a bonus action to magically manifest an echo of yourself in an unoccupied space you can see within 15 feet of you. This echo is a magical, translucent, gray image of you that lasts until it is destroyed, until you dismiss it as a bonus action, until you manifest another echo, or until you\\u0027re incapacitated.\\n\\nYour echo has AC 14 + your proficiency bonus, 1 hit point, and immunity to all conditions. If it has to make a saving throw, it uses your saving throw bonus for the roll. It is the same size as you, and it occupies its space. On your turn, you can mentally command the echo to move up to 30 feet in any direction (no action required). If your echo is ever more than 30 feet from you at the end of your turn, it is destroyed.\\n\\nYou can use the echo in the following ways:\\n\\n- As a bonus action, you can teleport, magically swapping places with your echo at a cost of 15 feet of your movement, regardless of the distance between the two of you.\\n\\n- When you take the Attack action on your turn, any attack you make with that action can originate from your space or the echo\\u0027s space. You make this choice for each attack.\\n\\n- When a creature that you can see within 5 feet of your echo moves at least 5 feet away from it, you can use your reaction to make an opportunity attack against that creature as if you were in the echo\\u0027s space\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom3635fae2-6bbb-41f5-8173-8dc95f07153e\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Manifest Echo\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can heighten your echo\\u0027s fury. Whenever you take the Attack action, you can make one additional melee attack from the echo\\u0027s position.\\n\\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier (a minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Custom8b81123f-d6d8-4fe4-a3cc-8dc770c71a5a\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Unleash Incarnation\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can temporarily transfer your consciousness to your echo. As an action, you can see through your echo\\u0027s eyes and hear through its ears. During this time, you are deafened and blinded. You can sustain this effect for up to 10 minutes, and you can end it at any time (requires no action). While your echo is being used in this way, it can be up to 1,000 feet away from you without being destroyed\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Customcacb0678-49e8-4b5d-a2c8-7b41dc19bbd5\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Echo Avatar\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can make your echo throw itself in front of an attack directed at another creature that you can see. Before the attack roll is made, you can use your reaction to teleport the echo to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the targeted creature. The attack roll that triggered the reaction is instead made against your echo.\\n\\nOnce you use this feature, you can\\u0027t use it again until you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":10}],\"id\":\"Customed887262-10d5-46b7-b659-ef8189ca1cf3\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Shadow Martyr\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":10},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You\\u0027ve learned to absorb the fleeting magic of your echo. When an echo of yours is destroyed by taking damage, you can gain a number of temporary hit points equal to 2d6 + your Constitution modifier, provided you don\\u0027t already have temporary hit points.\\n\\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier (a minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Custom71eede10-c30b-47a2-a8a3-3778e692f20c\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Reclaim Potential\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can use a bonus action to create two echoes with your Manifest Echo feature, and these echoes can coexist. If you try to create a third echo, the previous two echoes are destroyed. Anything you can do from one echo\\u0027s position can be done from the other\\u0027s instead.\\n\\nIn addition, when you roll initiative and have no uses of your Unleash Incarnation feature left, you regain one use of that feature\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Customd70e2bf9-0770-415b-9ff2-ae69e0ff739a\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Legion of One\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":18}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter_echo_knight\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Echo Knight\",\"selectableFeatures\":[],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[{\"abilityCalculators\":[{\"calculators\":[{\"operands\":[{\"multiplierConstant\":1,\"operator\":\"PLUS\",\"stat\":\"CON\"}]},{\"operands\":[{\"multiplierConstant\":1,\"operator\":\"PLUS\"}]}],\"level\":3,\"topLevelConnector\":\"MAX\"}],\"amountsPerLevel\":[],\"associatedValueName\":\"\",\"id\":\"c0e35d42-3cc6-4a06-b443-bab4b6c053a9\",\"name\":\"Unleash Incarnation Uses\",\"type\":\"ADVANCED\",\"usesLeft\":0},{\"abilityCalculators\":[{\"calculators\":[{\"operands\":[{\"multiplierConstant\":1,\"operator\":\"PLUS\",\"stat\":\"CON\"}]},{\"operands\":[{\"multiplierConstant\":1,\"operator\":\"PLUS\"}]}],\"level\":15,\"topLevelConnector\":\"MAX\"}],\"amountsPerLevel\":[],\"associatedValueName\":\"\",\"id\":\"09c003cb-e0ba-4915-aaad-eef20a47b124\",\"name\":\"Reclaim Potential Uses\",\"type\":\"ADVANCED\",\"usesLeft\":0}],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You harbor a wellspring of psionic energy within yourself. This energy is represented by your Psionic Energy dice, which are each a d6. You have a number of these dice equal to twice your proficiency bonus, and they fuel various psionic powers you have, which are detailed below.\\n\\nSome of your powers expend the Psionic Energy die they use, as specified in a power\\u0027s description, and you can\\u0027t use a power if it requires you to use a die when your dice are all expended. You regain all your expended Psionic Energy dice when you finish a long rest. In addition, as a bonus action, you can regain one expended Psionic Energy die, but you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest.\\n\\nThe powers below use your Psionic Energy dice.\\n\\n- Protective Field: When you or another creature you can see within 30 feet of you takes damage, you can use your reaction to expend one Psionic Energy die, roll the die, and reduce the damage taken by the number rolled plus your Intelligence modifier (minimum reduction of 1), as you create a momentary shield of telekinetic force.\\n\\n- Psionic Strike: You can propel your weapons with psionic force. Once on each of your turns, immediately after you hit a target within 30 feet of you with an attack and deal damage to it with a weapon, you can expend one Psionic Energy die, rolling it and dealing force damage to the target equal to the number rolled plus your Intelligence modifier.\\n\\n- Telekinetic Movement: You can move an object or a creature with your mind. As an action, you target one loose object that is Large or smaller or one willing creature, other than yourself. If you can see the target and it is within 30 feet of you, you can move it up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. Alternatively, if it is a Tiny object, you can move it to or from your hand. Either way, you can move the target horizontally, vertically, or both. Once you take this action, you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest, unless you expend a Psionic Energy die to take it again.\",\"level\":3},{\"description\":\"You harbor a wellspring of psionic energy within yourself. This energy is represented by your Psionic Energy dice, which are each a d8. You have a number of these dice equal to twice your proficiency bonus, and they fuel various psionic powers you have, which are detailed below.\\n\\nSome of your powers expend the Psionic Energy die they use, as specified in a power\\u0027s description, and you can\\u0027t use a power if it requires you to use a die when your dice are all expended. You regain all your expended Psionic Energy dice when you finish a long rest. In addition, as a bonus action, you can regain one expended Psionic Energy die, but you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest.\\n\\nThe powers below use your Psionic Energy dice.\\n\\n- Protective Field: When you or another creature you can see within 30 feet of you takes damage, you can use your reaction to expend one Psionic Energy die, roll the die, and reduce the damage taken by the number rolled plus your Intelligence modifier (minimum reduction of 1), as you create a momentary shield of telekinetic force.\\n\\n- Psionic Strike: You can propel your weapons with psionic force. Once on each of your turns, immediately after you hit a target within 30 feet of you with an attack and deal damage to it with a weapon, you can expend one Psionic Energy die, rolling it and dealing force damage to the target equal to the number rolled plus your Intelligence modifier.\\n\\n- Telekinetic Movement: You can move an object or a creature with your mind. As an action, you target one loose object that is Large or smaller or one willing creature, other than yourself. If you can see the target and it is within 30 feet of you, you can move it up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. Alternatively, if it is a Tiny object, you can move it to or from your hand. Either way, you can move the target horizontally, vertically, or both. Once you take this action, you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest, unless you expend a Psionic Energy die to take it again.\",\"level\":5},{\"description\":\"You harbor a wellspring of psionic energy within yourself. This energy is represented by your Psionic Energy dice, which are each a d8. You have a number of these dice equal to twice your proficiency bonus, and they fuel various psionic powers you have, which are detailed below.\\n\\nSome of your powers expend the Psionic Energy die they use, as specified in a power\\u0027s description, and you can\\u0027t use a power if it requires you to use a die when your dice are all expended. You regain all your expended Psionic Energy dice when you finish a long rest. In addition, as a bonus action, you can regain one expended Psionic Energy die, but you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest.\\n\\nThe powers below use your Psionic Energy dice.\\n\\n- Protective Field: When you or another creature you can see within 30 feet of you takes damage, you can use your reaction to expend one Psionic Energy die, roll the die, and reduce the damage taken by the number rolled plus your Intelligence modifier (minimum reduction of 1), as you create a momentary shield of telekinetic force.\\n\\n- Psionic Strike: You can propel your weapons with psionic force. Once on each of your turns, immediately after you hit a target within 30 feet of you with an attack and deal damage to it with a weapon, you can expend one Psionic Energy die, rolling it and dealing force damage to the target equal to the number rolled plus your Intelligence modifier.\\n\\n- Telekinetic Movement: You can move an object or a creature with your mind. As an action, you target one loose object that is Large or smaller or one willing creature, other than yourself. If you can see the target and it is within 30 feet of you, you can move it up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. Alternatively, if it is a Tiny object, you can move it to or from your hand. Either way, you can move the target horizontally, vertically, or both. Once you take this action, you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest, unless you expend a Psionic Energy die to take it again.\\n\\n- Psi-Powered Leap: As a bonus action, you can propel your body with your mind. You gain a flying speed equal to twice your walking speed until the end of the current turn. Once you take this bonus action, you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest, unless you expend a Psionic Energy die to take it again.\\n\\n- Telekinetic Thrust: When you deal damage to a target with your Psionic Strike, you can force the target to make a Strength saving throw against a DC equal to 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Intelligence modifier. If the save fails, you can knock the target prone or move it up to 10 feet in any direction horizontally.\",\"level\":7},{\"description\":\"You harbor a wellspring of psionic energy within yourself. This energy is represented by your Psionic Energy dice, which are each a d10. You have a number of these dice equal to twice your proficiency bonus, and they fuel various psionic powers you have, which are detailed below.\\n\\nSome of your powers expend the Psionic Energy die they use, as specified in a power\\u0027s description, and you can\\u0027t use a power if it requires you to use a die when your dice are all expended. You regain all your expended Psionic Energy dice when you finish a long rest. In addition, as a bonus action, you can regain one expended Psionic Energy die, but you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest.\\n\\nThe powers below use your Psionic Energy dice.\\n\\n- Protective Field: When you or another creature you can see within 30 feet of you takes damage, you can use your reaction to expend one Psionic Energy die, roll the die, and reduce the damage taken by the number rolled plus your Intelligence modifier (minimum reduction of 1), as you create a momentary shield of telekinetic force.\\n\\n- Psionic Strike: You can propel your weapons with psionic force. Once on each of your turns, immediately after you hit a target within 30 feet of you with an attack and deal damage to it with a weapon, you can expend one Psionic Energy die, rolling it and dealing force damage to the target equal to the number rolled plus your Intelligence modifier.\\n\\n- Telekinetic Movement: You can move an object or a creature with your mind. As an action, you target one loose object that is Large or smaller or one willing creature, other than yourself. If you can see the target and it is within 30 feet of you, you can move it up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. Alternatively, if it is a Tiny object, you can move it to or from your hand. Either way, you can move the target horizontally, vertically, or both. Once you take this action, you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest, unless you expend a Psionic Energy die to take it again.\\n\\n- Psi-Powered Leap: As a bonus action, you can propel your body with your mind. You gain a flying speed equal to twice your walking speed until the end of the current turn. Once you take this bonus action, you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest, unless you expend a Psionic Energy die to take it again.\\n\\n- Telekinetic Thrust: When you deal damage to a target with your Psionic Strike, you can force the target to make a Strength saving throw against a DC equal to 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Intelligence modifier. If the save fails, you can knock the target prone or move it up to 10 feet in any direction horizontally.\",\"level\":11},{\"description\":\"You harbor a wellspring of psionic energy within yourself. This energy is represented by your Psionic Energy dice, which are each a d12. You have a number of these dice equal to twice your proficiency bonus, and they fuel various psionic powers you have, which are detailed below.\\n\\nSome of your powers expend the Psionic Energy die they use, as specified in a power\\u0027s description, and you can\\u0027t use a power if it requires you to use a die when your dice are all expended. You regain all your expended Psionic Energy dice when you finish a long rest. In addition, as a bonus action, you can regain one expended Psionic Energy die, but you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest.\\n\\nThe powers below use your Psionic Energy dice.\\n\\n- Protective Field: When you or another creature you can see within 30 feet of you takes damage, you can use your reaction to expend one Psionic Energy die, roll the die, and reduce the damage taken by the number rolled plus your Intelligence modifier (minimum reduction of 1), as you create a momentary shield of telekinetic force.\\n\\n- Psionic Strike: You can propel your weapons with psionic force. Once on each of your turns, immediately after you hit a target within 30 feet of you with an attack and deal damage to it with a weapon, you can expend one Psionic Energy die, rolling it and dealing force damage to the target equal to the number rolled plus your Intelligence modifier.\\n\\n- Telekinetic Movement: You can move an object or a creature with your mind. As an action, you target one loose object that is Large or smaller or one willing creature, other than yourself. If you can see the target and it is within 30 feet of you, you can move it up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. Alternatively, if it is a Tiny object, you can move it to or from your hand. Either way, you can move the target horizontally, vertically, or both. Once you take this action, you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest, unless you expend a Psionic Energy die to take it again.\\n\\n- Psi-Powered Leap: As a bonus action, you can propel your body with your mind. You gain a flying speed equal to twice your walking speed until the end of the current turn. Once you take this bonus action, you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest, unless you expend a Psionic Energy die to take it again.\\n\\n- Telekinetic Thrust: When you deal damage to a target with your Psionic Strike, you can force the target to make a Strength saving throw against a DC equal to 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Intelligence modifier. If the save fails, you can knock the target prone or move it up to 10 feet in any direction horizontally.\",\"level\":17}],\"id\":\"Customb06cc5e7-80cd-4c35-bd32-15f806690c55\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Psionic Power\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain new ways to use your telekinetic abilities\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Custom99c65370-1da4-4259-85b2-fa9f0e6f1c0c\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Telekinetic Adept\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"The psionic energy flowing through you has bolstered your mind. You have resistance to psychic damage. Moreover, if you start your turn charmed or frightened, you can expend a Psionic Energy die and end every effect on yourself subjecting you to those conditions\",\"level\":10}],\"id\":\"Custom3a263dae-2470-4ccd-ad14-800ba29764c4\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Guarded Mind\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":10},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can shield yourself and others with telekinetic force. As a bonus action, you can choose creatures, which can include you, that you can see within 30 feet of you, up to a number of creatures equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of one creature). Each of the chosen creatures is protected by half cover for 1 minute or until you\\u0027re incapacitated.\\n\\nOnce you take this bonus action, you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a long rest, unless you expend a Psionic Energy die to take it again\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Customc7fd8437-eb81-4546-806e-b5e3d8898d96\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Bulwark of Force\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Your ability to move creatures and objects with your mind is matched by few. You can cast the telekinesis spell, requiring no components, and your spellcasting ability for the spell is Intelligence. On each of your turns while you concentrate on the spell, including the turn when you cast it, you can make one attack with a weapon as a bonus action.\\n\\nOnce you cast the spell with this feature, you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a long rest, unless you expend a Psionic Energy die to cast it again\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Customca2ee7f9-2062-4901-9be8-f9105d0e5cfc\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Telekinetic Master\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":18}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter_psi_warrior_[tce]\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Psi Warrior [TCE]\",\"selectableFeatures\":[],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[{\"abilityCalculators\":[{\"associatedValue\":\"d6\",\"calculators\":[{\"operands\":[{\"multiplierConstant\":2,\"operator\":\"PLUS\",\"stat\":\"PB\"}]}],\"level\":3,\"topLevelConnector\":\"MAX\"},{\"associatedValue\":\"d8\",\"calculators\":[{\"operands\":[{\"multiplierConstant\":2,\"operator\":\"PLUS\",\"stat\":\"PB\"}]}],\"level\":5,\"topLevelConnector\":\"MAX\"},{\"associatedValue\":\"d10\",\"calculators\":[{\"operands\":[{\"multiplierConstant\":2,\"operator\":\"PLUS\",\"stat\":\"PB\"}]}],\"level\":11,\"topLevelConnector\":\"MAX\"},{\"associatedValue\":\"d12\",\"calculators\":[{\"operands\":[{\"multiplierConstant\":2,\"operator\":\"PLUS\",\"stat\":\"PB\"}]}],\"level\":17,\"topLevelConnector\":\"MAX\"}],\"amountsPerLevel\":[],\"associatedValueName\":\"Die\",\"id\":\"1cdd36dc-069f-4c1a-9b7b-18bc350f7acb\",\"name\":\"Psionic Dice\",\"type\":\"ADVANCED\",\"usesLeft\":0}],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[{\"level\":18,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"sorcerer, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, S\",\"description\":\"You gain the ability to move or manipulate Creatures or Objects by thought. When you cast the spell, and as your Action each round for the Duration, you can exert your will on one creature or object that you can see within range, causing the appropriate Effect below. You can affect the same target round after round, or choose a new one at any time. If you switch Targets, the prior target is no longer affected by the spell.\\n\\nCreature: You can try to move a Huge or smaller creature. Make an ability check with your Spellcasting ability contested by the creature\\u0027s Strength check. If you win the contest, you move the creature up to 30 feet in any direction, including upward but not beyond the range of this spell. Until the end of your next turn, the creature is Restrained in your Telekinetic grip. A creature lifted upward is suspended in mid-air.\\n\\nOn subsequent rounds, you can use your Action to attempt to maintain your Telekinetic grip on the creature by repeating the contest.\\n\\nObject: You can try to move an object that weighs up to 1,000 pounds. If the object isn\\u0027t being worn or carried, you automatically move it up to 30 feet in any direction, but not beyond the range of this spell.\\n\\nIf the object is worn or carried by a creature, you must make an ability check with your Spellcasting ability contested by that creature\\u0027s Strength check. If you succeed, you pull the object away from that creature and can move it up to 30 feet in any direction but not beyond the range of this spell.\\n\\nYou can exert fine control on Objects with your Telekinetic grip, such as manipulating a simple tool, opening a door or a container, stowing or retrieving an item from an open container, or pouring the Contents from a vial\",\"duration\":\"Concentration, up to 10 minutes\",\"higherLevels\":\"\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":5,\"name\":\"Telekinesis\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"60 feet\",\"school\":\"transmutation\",\"type\":\"5th-level transmutation\"}}],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can use magic runes to enhance your gear. You know 2 runes of your choice, from among the runes described below, and each time you gain a level in this class, you can replace one rune you know with a different one from this feature.\\n\\nWhenever you finish a long rest, you can touch a number of objects equal to the number of runes you know, and you inscribe a different rune onto each of the objects. To be eligible, an object must be a weapon, a suit of armor, a shield, a piece of jewelry, or something else you can wear or hold in a hand. Your rune remains on an object until you finish a long rest, and an object can bear only one of your runes at a time.\\n\\nIf a rune has a level requirement, you must be at least that level in this class to learn the rune. If a rune requires a saving throw, your Rune Magic save DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier\",\"level\":3},{\"description\":\"You can use magic runes to enhance your gear. You know 3 runes of your choice, from among the runes described below, and each time you gain a level in this class, you can replace one rune you know with a different one from this feature.\\n\\nWhenever you finish a long rest, you can touch a number of objects equal to the number of runes you know, and you inscribe a different rune onto each of the objects. To be eligible, an object must be a weapon, a suit of armor, a shield, a piece of jewelry, or something else you can wear or hold in a hand. Your rune remains on an object until you finish a long rest, and an object can bear only one of your runes at a time.\\n\\nIf a rune has a level requirement, you must be at least that level in this class to learn the rune. If a rune requires a saving throw, your Rune Magic save DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier\",\"level\":7},{\"description\":\"You can use magic runes to enhance your gear. You know 4 runes of your choice, from among the runes described below, and each time you gain a level in this class, you can replace one rune you know with a different one from this feature.\\n\\nWhenever you finish a long rest, you can touch a number of objects equal to the number of runes you know, and you inscribe a different rune onto each of the objects. To be eligible, an object must be a weapon, a suit of armor, a shield, a piece of jewelry, or something else you can wear or hold in a hand. Your rune remains on an object until you finish a long rest, and an object can bear only one of your runes at a time.\\n\\nIf a rune has a level requirement, you must be at least that level in this class to learn the rune. If a rune requires a saving throw, your Rune Magic save DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"You can use magic runes to enhance your gear. You know 5 runes of your choice, from among the runes described below, and each time you gain a level in this class, you can replace one rune you know with a different one from this feature.\\n\\nWhenever you finish a long rest, you can touch a number of objects equal to the number of runes you know, and you inscribe a different rune onto each of the objects. To be eligible, an object must be a weapon, a suit of armor, a shield, a piece of jewelry, or something else you can wear or hold in a hand. Your rune remains on an object until you finish a long rest, and an object can bear only one of your runes at a time.\\n\\nIf a rune has a level requirement, you must be at least that level in this class to learn the rune. If a rune requires a saving throw, your Rune Magic save DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Custom07356dc2-00b9-4b14-8ed6-c433f5f09561\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Rune Carver\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"As a bonus action, you magically gain the following benefits, which last for 1 minute:\\n\\n- If you are smaller than Large, you become Large, along with anything you are wearing. If you lack the room to become Large, your size doesn\\u0027t change.\\n\\n- You have advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws.\\n\\n- Once on each of your turns, one of your attacks with a weapon or an unarmed strike can deal an extra 1d6 damage to a target on a hit.\\n\\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a long rest\",\"level\":3},{\"description\":\"As a bonus action, you magically gain the following benefits, which last for 1 minute:\\n\\n- If you are smaller than Large, you become Large, along with anything you are wearing. If you lack the room to become Large, your size doesn\\u0027t change.\\n\\n- You have advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws.\\n\\n- Once on each of your turns, one of your attacks with a weapon or an unarmed strike can deal an extra 1d8 damage to a target on a hit.\\n\\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a long rest\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"As a bonus action, you magically gain the following benefits, which last for 1 minute:\\n\\n- If you are smaller than Huge, you become Huge, along with anything you are wearing, and your reach increases by 5 ft. If you lack the room to become Huge, your size doesn\\u0027t change.\\n\\n- You have advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws.\\n\\n- Once on each of your turns, one of your attacks with a weapon or an unarmed strike can deal an extra 1d10 damage to a target on a hit.\\n\\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a long rest\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom3e601c40-4557-4ffa-8639-ecb1a638f9ee\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Giant\\u0027s Might\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You learn to invoke your rune magic to protect your allies. When another creature you can see within 60 feet of you is hit by an attack roll, you can use your reaction to force the attacker to reroll the d20 and use the new roll.\\n\\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Custom6fceb122-c8cb-4190-8f0e-4a22e1dad9b8\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Runic Shield\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"The magic of your runes permanently alters you. When you gain this feature, roll 3d4. You grow a number of inches in height equal to the roll\",\"level\":10}],\"id\":\"Custome79f0134-52ee-4f4a-a8e6-9af9399837da\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Great Stature\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":10},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can invoke each rune you know from your Rune Carver feature twice, rather than once, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Customb70b939d-c7c5-4f69-a586-bb8dfa466572\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Master of Runes\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You learn how to amplify your rune-powered transformation, and therefore the details of your Giant\\u0027s Might feature have been updated\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom29fb73c1-2e8e-49fc-ba61-d1677bbd3b3a\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Runic Juggernaut\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":18}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter_rune_knight_[tce]\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[{\"hint\":\"\",\"level\":1,\"proficiency\":\"Giant\"}],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Rune Knight [TCE]\",\"selectableFeatures\":[{\"amountsPerLevel\":[{\"amount\":2,\"level\":3},{\"amount\":3,\"level\":7},{\"amount\":4,\"level\":10},{\"amount\":5,\"level\":15}],\"availableFeatures\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, you have advantage on Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) checks and Charisma (Deception) checks.\\n\\nIn addition, when you or a creature you can see within 30 feet of you is hit by an attack roll, you can use your reaction to invoke the rune and choose a different creature within 30 feet of you, other than the attacker. The chosen creature becomes the target of the attack, using the same roll. This magic can transfer the attack\\u0027s effects regardless of the attack\\u0027s range.\\n\\nOnce you invoke this rune, you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom167f2c84-fc80-487e-84f4-4559bae5d7cf\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Cloud Rune\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, your proficiency bonus is doubled for any ability check you make that uses your proficiency with a tool.\\n\\nIn addition, when you hit a creature with an attack using a weapon, you can invoke the rune to summon fiery shackles: the target takes an extra 2d6 fire damage, and it must succeed on a Strength saving throw or be restrained for 1 minute. While restrained by the shackles, the target takes 2d6 fire damage at the start of each of its turns. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, banishing the shackles on a success.\\n\\nOnce you invoke this rune, you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customb02607bc-b051-451e-946d-799cda21c96d\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Fire Rune\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, you have advantage on Wisdom (Animal Handling) checks and Charisma (Intimidation) checks.\\n\\nIn addition, you can invoke the rune as a bonus action to increase your sturdiness. For 10 minutes, you gain a +2 bonus to all ability checks and saving throws that use Strength or Constitution.\\n\\nOnce you invoke this rune, you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customf8fdf717-dae0-44f7-9ffb-c1fddb0900c8\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Frost Rune\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, you have advantage on Wisdom (Insight) checks, and you have darkvision out to a range of 120 feet.\\n\\nIn addition, when a creature you can see ends its turn within 30 feet of you, you can use your reaction to invoke the rune and force the creature to make a Wisdom saving throw. Unless the save succeeds, the creature is charmed by you for 1 minute. While charmed in this way, the creature has a speed of 0 and is incapacitated, descending into a dreamy stupor. The creature repeats the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.\\n\\nOnce you invoke this rune, you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custome9aaa844-5f8f-4f49-8d3a-21ac65e2514f\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Stone Rune\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"While wearing or carrying an object that bears this rune, you have advantage on saving throws against being poisoned, and you have resistance against poison damage.\\n\\nIn addition, you can invoke the rune as a bonus action, gaining resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage for 1 minute.\\n\\nOnce you invoke this rune, you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Custom850cdbfa-22d6-4061-b3b2-d5840bf9a2ba\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Hill Rune\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, you have advantage on Intelligence (Arcana) checks, and you can\\u0027t be surprised as long as you aren\\u0027t incapacitated.\\n\\nIn addition, you can invoke the rune as a bonus action to enter a prophetic state for 1 minute or until you\\u0027re incapacitated. Until the state ends, when you or another creature you can see within 60 feet of you makes an attack roll, a saving throw, or an ability check, you can use your reaction to cause the roll to have advantage or disadvantage.\\n\\nOnce you invoke this rune, you can\\u0027t do so again until you finish a short or long rest\",\"level\":7}],\"id\":\"Custom5bbee7e9-e68a-48b5-af9d-9abc5a861c04\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Storm Rune\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7}],\"canReselect\":true,\"id\":\"224ea893-b45e-4db2-905d-ad133e23b838\",\"name\":\"Known Runes\",\"selectedFeatures\":[]}],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[{\"abilityCalculators\":[{\"calculators\":[{\"operands\":[{\"multiplierConstant\":1,\"operator\":\"PLUS\",\"stat\":\"PB\"}]}],\"level\":3,\"topLevelConnector\":\"MAX\"}],\"amountsPerLevel\":[],\"associatedValueName\":\"\",\"id\":\"fe09a0c6-43a5-470e-b954-0fd48fc78d70\",\"name\":\"Giant\\u0027s Might Uses\",\"type\":\"ADVANCED\",\"usesLeft\":0},{\"abilityCalculators\":[{\"calculators\":[{\"operands\":[{\"multiplierConstant\":1,\"operator\":\"PLUS\",\"stat\":\"PB\"}]}],\"level\":7,\"topLevelConnector\":\"MAX\"}],\"amountsPerLevel\":[],\"associatedValueName\":\"\",\"id\":\"182d017d-6193-4a11-80fc-e114944657ef\",\"name\":\"Runic Shield Uses\",\"type\":\"ADVANCED\",\"usesLeft\":0}],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[{\"hint\":\"\",\"level\":1,\"proficiency\":\"Smith\\u0027s tools\"}],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"Custom070af439-26ec-42aa-ada6-8f1e8f050ffd\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Guerreiro Lírico \",\"selectableFeatures\":[],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Você gasta uma hora transformando qualquer instrumento musical em um instrumento mágico. Esse instrumento magico tem diversas magias que podem ser acopladas em seus módulos. O usuário pode escolher 2 magias por módulo, podendo mudá-las quando sobe de nível.\\n\\nMódulo Suporte: Shield, Healing Word, Divine Favor ou Bless\\n\\nMódulo Ataque: Magic Missile, Witch Bolt, Arms of Hadar ou Charm Person\\n\\nAs magias do módulo Suporte podem ser usadas tanto no usuário quanto em aliados.\\n\\nO atributo de ataque das magias é o Carisma, e pode se usar 3 vezes cada módulo antes de um descanso longo.\",\"level\":3},{\"description\":\"A magia Crown of Madness pode ser adicionadas no Módulo de Ataque como escolha e a magia Prayer of Healing no Módulo de Suporte.\",\"level\":7},{\"description\":\"Agora cada módulo pode ser usado 5 vezes antes de um descanso longo e as 4 magias de cada módulo podem ser utilizadas.\",\"level\":10}],\"id\":\"Customd9625a9d-c3d6-49f2-a113-2a3f958a308a\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Instrumento Bélico\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Como ação bônus no seu turno, você pode adicionar 1d6 tanto nas jogadas de ataque e de dano do seu próximo ataque ou no próximo ataque de um aliado. Assim que usada essa característica, é necessário um descanso curto para utilizá-la novamente.\\n\",\"level\":7},{\"description\":\"O dado passa a ser 2d6 e esta característica pode ser usada 3 antes de um descanso curto.\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"O dado passa a ser 2d8.\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Custom7710ccfb-fdc5-472b-b34d-67736c2133c3\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Inspiração Marcial\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"O usuário troca uma melodia em que todos inimigos que ele possa ver em 100 pés e que ele queira prejudicar tenham desvantagem nas sua próxima jogada de ataque ou teste de resistência. Ao invés disso o usuário pode escolher curar 2d8 + seu nivel em pontos de vida de quem ele quiser e possa ver em 100 pés ou dar vantagem nas suas próximas jogadas de ataque ou teste de resistência (uma só).\\n\\nAssim que usada, o usuário deve ter um descanço longo a fim de recuperar esta característica.\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"Você pode usar essa habilidade 3 vezes antes de um descanso longo.\",\"level\":15},{\"description\":\"As vantagens e desvantagens duram pelos próximos 3 ataques ou testes de quem foi afetado. Você pode usar essa habilidade 5 vezes antes de um descanso longo.\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custombf23ca47-d6cb-4393-a909-ad6aaac97483\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Melodia Desconcertante\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":10},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"O seu Instrumento Bélico recebe uma melhoria, podendo suportar novas magias em seus módulos.\\n\\nMódulo de Suporte: Circle of Power, Mass Cure Wounds ou Teleportation Cicle.\\n\\nMódulo de Ataque: Destructive Wave,  Modify Memory ou Insect Plague.\\n\\nSomente uma magia dessas pode ser utilizada em cada módulo e só pode ser usada 1 vez por descanso longo.\",\"level\":15},{\"description\":\"Você pode escolher 3 magias de cada módulo. Agora podera usar 3 vezes as magia de cada módulo por descanso longo.\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Customaa7fbe82-43cf-45ae-b6a5-2e6196a58b2d\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Melhoria Lírica\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"O seu Instrumento Bélico recebe uma melhoria que suporta uma arma ser acoplada nele, possibilitando o usuário conjurar uma magia e atacar com sua arma na mesma ação.\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom5b8b48fb-0035-47b3-be66-bb3eb071c046\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Armação Bélica\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":18}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"Custom79233256-7bb1-4d1f-af0d-ddf800c16203\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":true,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Guerreiro Lírico\",\"selectableFeatures\":[],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Charisma\",\"spells\":[{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 reaction, which you take when you are hit by an attack or targeted by the magic missile spell\",\"classes\":\"sorcerer, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, S\",\"description\":\"An invisible barrier of magical force appears and protects you. Until the start of your next turn, you have a +5 bonus to AC, including against the triggering attack, and you take no damage from magic missile.\",\"duration\":\"1 round\",\"higherLevels\":\"\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Shield\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"Self\",\"school\":\"abjuration\",\"type\":\"1st-level abjuration\"}},{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 bonus action\",\"classes\":\"bard, cleric, druid\",\"components\":\"V\",\"description\":\"A creature of your choice that you can see within range regains hit points equal to 1d4 + your spellcasting ability modifier. This spell has no effect on undead or constructs.\",\"duration\":\"Instantaneous\",\"higherLevels\":\"When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 2nd level or higher, the healing increases by 1d4 for each slot level above 1st.\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Healing Word\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"60 feet\",\"school\":\"evocation\",\"type\":\"1st-level evocation\"}},{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 bonus action\",\"classes\":\"paladin\",\"components\":\"V, S\",\"description\":\"Your prayer empowers you with divine radiance. Until the spell ends, your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d4 radiant damage on a hit.\",\"duration\":\"Concentration, up to 1 minute\",\"higherLevels\":\"\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Divine Favor\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"Self\",\"school\":\"evocation\",\"type\":\"1st-level evocation\"}},{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"sorcerer, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, S\",\"description\":\"You create three glowing darts of magical force. Each dart hits a creature of your choice that you can see within range. A dart deals 1d4 + 1 force damage to its target. The darts all strike simultaneously, and you can direct them to hit one creature or several.\",\"duration\":\"Instantaneous\",\"higherLevels\":\"When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 2nd level or higher, the spell creates one more dart for each slot level above 1st.\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Magic Missile\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"120 feet\",\"school\":\"evocation\",\"type\":\"1st-level evocation\"}},{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"warlock, blood_hunter\",\"components\":\"V S M (Pickled octopus tentacle)\",\"description\":\"A 20-foot-radius void appears. It\\u0027s filled with whispers and slurping that can be heard up to 30 feet away. No light can illuminate the area, and creatures fully in it are blinded. The void\\u0027s area is difficult terrain. Any creature that starts its turn in the area takes 2d6 cold damage. Any creature that ends its turn there must pass a Dexterity save or take 2d6 acid damage.\",\"duration\":\"Concentration. Up to 1 minute\",\"higherLevels\":\"\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":3,\"name\":\"Hunger of Hadar\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"150 feet\",\"school\":\"conjuration\",\"type\":\"3rd-level conjuration\"}},{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"sorcerer, warlock, blood_hunter, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, S, M (a twig from a tree that has been struck by lightning)\",\"description\":\"A beam of crackling, blue energy lances out toward a creature within range, forming a sustained arc of lightning between you and the target. Make a ranged spell attack against that creature. On a hit, the target takes 1d12 lightning damage, and on each of your turns for the duration, you can use your action to deal 1d12 lightning damage to the target automatically. The spell ends if you use your action to do anything else. The spell also ends if the target is ever outside the spell\\u0027s range or if it has total cover from you.\",\"duration\":\"Concentration, up to 1 minute\",\"higherLevels\":\"When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 2nd level or higher, the damage increases by 1d12 for each slot level above 1st.\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Witch Bolt\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"30 feet\",\"school\":\"evocation\",\"type\":\"1st-level evocation\"}},{\"level\":7,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"bard, sorcerer, warlock, blood_hunter, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, S\",\"description\":\"One humanoid of your choice that you can see within range must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or become charmed by you for the duration. While the target is charmed in this way, a twisted crown of jagged iron appears on its head, and a madness glows in its eyes. The charmed target must use its action before moving on each of its turns to make a melee attack against a creature other than itself that you mentally choose. The target can act normally on its turn if you choose no creature or if none are within its reach.\\n\\nOn your subsequent turns, you must use your action to maintain control over the target, or the spell ends. Also, the target can make a Wisdom saving throw at the end of each of its turns. On a success, the spell ends\",\"duration\":\"Concentration, up to 1 minute\",\"higherLevels\":\"\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":2,\"name\":\"Crown of Madness\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"120 feet\",\"school\":\"enchantment\",\"type\":\"2nd-Level enchantment\"}},{\"level\":7,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"10 minutes\",\"classes\":\"cleric\",\"components\":\"V\",\"description\":\"Up to six creatures of your choice that you can see within range each regain hit points equal to 2d8 + your spellcasting ability modifier. This spell has no effect on undead or constructs.\",\"duration\":\"Instantaneous\",\"higherLevels\":\"When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 3rd level or higher, the healing increases by 1d8 for each slot level above 2nd.\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":2,\"name\":\"Prayer of Healing\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"30 feet\",\"school\":\"evocation\",\"type\":\"2nd-level evocation\"}},{\"level\":15,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"bard, sorcerer, warlock, blood_hunter, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, M (a snake\\u0027s tongue and either a bit of honeycomb or a drop of sweet oil)\",\"description\":\"You suggest a course of activity (limited to a sentence or two) and magically influence up to twelve creatures of your choice that you can see within range and that can hear and understand you. Creatures that can\\u0027t be charmed are immune to this effect. The suggestion must be worded in such a manner as to make the course of action sound reasonable. Asking the creature to stab itself, throw itself onto a spear, immolate itself, or do some other obviously harmful act automatically negates the effect of the spell.\\n\\nEach target must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, it pursues the course of action you described to the best of its ability. The suggested course of action can continue for the entire duration. If the suggested activity can be completed in a shorter time, the spell ends when the subject finishes what it was asked to do.\\n\\nYou can also specify conditions that will trigger a special activity during the duration. For example, you might suggest that a group of soldiers give all their money to the first beggar they meet. If the condition isn\\u0027t met before the spell ends, the activity isn’t performed.\\n\\nIf you or any of your companions damage a creature affected by this spell, the spell ends for that creature.\",\"duration\":\"24 hours\",\"higherLevels\":\"When you cast this spell using a 7th-level spell slot, the duration is 10 days. When you use an 8th-level spell slot, the duration is 30 days. When you use a 9th-level spell slot, the duration is a year and a day.\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":6,\"name\":\"Mass Suggestion\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"60 feet\",\"school\":\"enchantment\",\"type\":\"6th-level enchantment\"}},{\"level\":15,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"druid\",\"components\":\"V, S\",\"description\":\"This spell creates a magical link between a Large or larger inanimate plant within range and another plant, at any distance, on the same plane of existence. You must have seen or touched the destination plant at least once before. For the duration, any creature can step into the target plant and exit from the destination plant by using 5 feet of movement.\",\"duration\":\"1 round\",\"higherLevels\":\"\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":6,\"name\":\"Transport via Plants\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"10 feet\",\"school\":\"conjuration\",\"type\":\"6th-level conjuration\"}},{\"level\":15,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"sorcerer, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, S\",\"description\":\"You create a 20-foot-radius sphere of poisonous, yellow-green fog centered on a point you choose within range. The fog spreads around corners. It lasts for the duration or until strong wind disperses the fog, ending the spell. Its area is heavily obscured.\\n\\nWhen a creature enters the spell\\u0027s area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, that creature must make a Constitution saving throw. The creature takes 5d8 poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Creatures are affected even if they hold their breath or don\\u0027t need to breathe.\\n\\nThe fog moves 10 feet away from you at the start of each of your turns, rolling along the surface of the ground. The vapors, being heavier than air, sink to the lowest level of the land, even pouring down openings.\",\"duration\":\"Concentration, up to 10 minutes\",\"higherLevels\":\"When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 6th level or higher, the damage increases by 1d8 for each slot level above 5th.\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":5,\"name\":\"Cloudkill\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"120 feet\",\"school\":\"conjuration\",\"type\":\"5th-level conjuration\"}},{\"level\":15,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"sorcerer, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, S, M (a lodestone and a pinch of dust)\",\"description\":\"A thin green ray springs from your pointing finger to a target that you can see within range. The target can be a creature, an object, or a Creation of magical force, such as the wall created by Wall of Force.\\n\\nA creature targeted by this spell must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes 10d6+40 force damage. If this damage reduces the target to 0 Hit Points, it is disintegrated.\\n\\nA disintegrated creature and everything it is wearing and carrying, except Magic Items, are reduced to a pile of fine gray dust. The creature can be restored to life only by means of a True Resurrection or a wish spell.\\n\\nThis spell automatically disintegrates a Large or smaller nonmagical object or a Creation of magical force. If the target is a Huge or larger object or Creation of force, this spell disintegrates a 10-foot-cube portion of it. A magic item is unaffected by this spell\",\"duration\":\"Instantaneous\",\"higherLevels\":\"When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 7th level or higher, the damage increases by 3d6 for each slot level above 6th\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":6,\"name\":\"Disintegrate\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"60 feet\",\"school\":\"transmutation\",\"type\":\"6th-level transmutation\"}},{\"level\":15,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"druid\",\"components\":\"V, S, M (several seeds of any moonseed plant and a piece of opalescent feldspar)\",\"description\":\"A silvery beam of pale light shines down in a 5-foot-radius, 40-foot-high cylinder centered on a point within range. Until the spell ends, dim light fills the cylinder.\\n\\nWhen a creature enters the spell\\u0027s area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, it is engulfed in ghostly flames that cause searing pain, and it must make a Constitution saving throw. It takes 2d10 radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much on a successful one.\\n\\nA shapechanger makes its saving throw with disadvantage. If it fails, it also instantly reverts to its original form and can\\u0027t assume a different form until it leaves the spells light.\\n\\nOn each of your turns after you cast this spell use can use an action to move the beam 60 feet in any direction.\",\"duration\":\"Concentration, up to 1 minute\",\"higherLevels\":\"When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 3rd level or higher, the damage increases by 1d10 for each slot level above 2nd.\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":2,\"name\":\"Moonbeam\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"120 feet\",\"school\":\"evocation\",\"type\":\"2nd-level evocation\"}},{\"level\":15,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"sorcerer, fighter, rogue, wizard, bard\",\"components\":\"V\",\"description\":\"Choose an object that you can see within range. The object can be a door, a box, a chest, a set of Manacles, a padlock, or another object that contains a mundane or magical means that prevents access.\\n\\nA target that is held shut by a mundane lock or that is stuck or barred becomes unlocked, unstuck, or unbarred. If the object has multiple locks, only one of them is unlocked.\\n\\nIf you choose a target that is held shut with Arcane Lock, that spell is suppressed for 10 minutes, during which time the target can be opened and shut normally.\\n\\nWhen you cast the spell, a loud knock, audible from as far away as 300 feet, emanates from the target object\",\"duration\":\"Instantaneous\",\"higherLevels\":\"\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":2,\"name\":\"Knock\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"60 feet\",\"school\":\"transmutation\",\"type\":\"2nd-level transmutation\"}},{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"cleric, paladin\",\"components\":\"V, S, M (a sprinkling of holy water)\",\"description\":\"You bless up to three creatures of your choice within range. Whenever a target makes an attack roll or a saving throw before the spell ends, the target can roll a d4 and add the number rolled to the attack roll or saving throw.\",\"duration\":\"Concentration, up to 1 minute\",\"higherLevels\":\"\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Bless\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"30 feet\",\"school\":\"enchantment\",\"type\":\"1st-level enchantment\"}},{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"bard, druid, sorcerer, warlock, blood_hunter, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, S\",\"description\":\"You attempt to charm a humanoid you can see within range. It must make a Wisdom saving throw, and does so with advantage if you or your companions are fighting it. If it fails the saving throw, it is charmed by you until the spell ends or until you or your companions do anything harmful to it. The charmed creature regards you as a friendly acquaintance. When the spell ends, the creature knows it was charmed by you.\",\"duration\":\"1 hour\",\"higherLevels\":\"When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 2nd level or higher, you can target one additional creature for each slot level above 1st. The creatures must be within 30 feet of each other when you target them.\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Charm Person\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"30 feet\",\"school\":\"enchantment\",\"type\":\"1st-level enchantment\"}}],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]},{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Você gasta uma hora transformando qualquer instrumento musical em um instrumento mágico. Esse instrumento magico tem diversas magias que podem ser acopladas em seus módulos. O usuário pode escolher 2 magias por módulo, podendo mudá-las quando sobe de nível.\\n\\nMódulo Suporte: Shield, Healing Word, Divine Favor ou Bless\\n\\nMódulo Ataque: Magic Missile, Witch Bolt, Arms of Hadar ou Charm Person\\n\\nAs magias do módulo Suporte podem ser usadas tanto no usuário quanto em aliados.\\n\\nO atributo de ataque das magias é o Carisma, e pode se usar 3 vezes cada módulo antes de um descanso longo.\",\"level\":3},{\"description\":\"Q magia Crown of Madness pode ser adicionadas no Módulo de Ataque como escolha e a magia Prayer of Healing no Módulo de Suporte.\",\"level\":7},{\"description\":\"Agora cada módulo pode ser usado 5 vezes antes de um descanso longo e as 4 magias de cada módulo podem ser utilizadas.\",\"level\":10}],\"id\":\"Custom4e9ff2a2-1603-4c6a-8c6c-70adc7a2c92a\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Instrumento Bélico \",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Como ação bônus no seu turno, você pode adicionar 1d6 tanto nas jogadas de ataque e de dano do seu próximo ataque ou no próximo ataque de um aliado. Assim que usada essa característica, é necessário um descanso curto para utilizá-la novamente.\",\"level\":7},{\"description\":\"O dado passa a ser 2d6 e esta característica pode ser usada 3 antes de um descanso curto.\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"O dado passa a ser 2d8.\",\"level\":15}],\"id\":\"Custom3553eb6c-4ee4-47ae-bc6e-3f1dfa705f53\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Inspiração Marcial\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":7},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"O usuário troca uma melodia em que todos inimigos que ele possa ver em 100 pés e que ele queira prejudicar tenham desvantagem nas sua próxima jogada de ataque ou teste de resistência. Ao invés disso o usuário pode escolher curar 2d8 + seu nivel em pontos de vida de quem ele quiser e possa ver em 100 pés ou dar vantagem nas suas próximas jogadas de ataque ou teste de resistência (uma só).\\n\\nAssim que usada, o usuário deve ter um descanço longo a fim de recuperar esta característica.\",\"level\":10},{\"description\":\"Você pode usar essa habilidade 3 vezes antes de um descanso longo.\",\"level\":15},{\"description\":\"As vantagens e desvantagens passam a ser nos próximos 3 ataques, e a cura fica 2d12 + seu nível. Você pode usar essa habilidade 5 vezes antes de um descanso longo.\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom7749fa50-4a36-4639-aeaf-6c3f95400d1f\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Melodia Desconcertante\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":10},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"O seu Instrumento Bélico recebe uma melhoria, podendo suportar novas magias em seus módulos.\\n\\nMódulo de Suporte: Circle of Power, Mass Cure Wounds ou Teleportation Cicle.\\n\\nMódulo de Ataque: Destructive Wave,  Modify Memory ou Insect Plague.\\n\\nSomente uma magia dessas pode ser utilizada em cada módulo e só pode ser usado 1 vez por descanso longo.\",\"level\":15},{\"description\":\"Você pode escolher 3 magias de cada módulo. Agora podera usar 3 vezes as magia de cada módulo por descanso longo.\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Custom4a9e4078-b856-4295-81f0-d30e0e8dc0fc\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Melhoria Lírica \",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":15},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"O seu Instrumento Bélico recebe uma melhoria que suporta uma arma ser acoplada nele, possibilitando o usuário conjurar uma magia e atacar com sua arma na mesma ação.\",\"level\":18}],\"id\":\"Customab869d4f-f7ac-46b5-988b-0e9c20d96b3a\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Armação Bélica \",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":18}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"Custom2efa5b98-e53e-401f-8d62-fa4a1972cf93\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Archetype\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":false,\"multiclassTools\":true,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Guerreiro Lírico \",\"selectableFeatures\":[],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[{\"hint\":\"\",\"level\":3,\"proficiency\":\"full,performance\"}],\"specialAbilities\":[],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Charisma\",\"spells\":[{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 bonus action\",\"classes\":\"bard, cleric, druid\",\"components\":\"V\",\"description\":\"A creature of your choice that you can see within range regains hit points equal to 1d4 + your spellcasting ability modifier. This spell has no effect on undead or constructs.\",\"duration\":\"Instantaneous\",\"higherLevels\":\"When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 2nd level or higher, the healing increases by 1d4 for each slot level above 1st.\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Healing Word\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"60 feet\",\"school\":\"evocation\",\"type\":\"1st-level evocation\"}},{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"cleric, paladin\",\"components\":\"V, S, M (a sprinkling of holy water)\",\"description\":\"You bless up to three creatures of your choice within range. Whenever a target makes an attack roll or a saving throw before the spell ends, the target can roll a d4 and add the number rolled to the attack roll or saving throw.\",\"duration\":\"Concentration, up to 1 minute\",\"higherLevels\":\"\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Bless\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"30 feet\",\"school\":\"enchantment\",\"type\":\"1st-level enchantment\"}},{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 reaction, which you take when you are hit by an attack or targeted by the magic missile spell\",\"classes\":\"sorcerer, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, S\",\"description\":\"An invisible barrier of magical force appears and protects you. Until the start of your next turn, you have a +5 bonus to AC, including against the triggering attack, and you take no damage from magic missile.\",\"duration\":\"1 round\",\"higherLevels\":\"\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Shield\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"Self\",\"school\":\"abjuration\",\"type\":\"1st-level abjuration\"}},{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 bonus action\",\"classes\":\"paladin\",\"components\":\"V, S\",\"description\":\"Your prayer empowers you with divine radiance. Until the spell ends, your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d4 radiant damage on a hit.\",\"duration\":\"Concentration, up to 1 minute\",\"higherLevels\":\"\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Divine Favor\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"Self\",\"school\":\"evocation\",\"type\":\"1st-level evocation\"}},{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"sorcerer, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, S\",\"description\":\"You create three glowing darts of magical force. Each dart hits a creature of your choice that you can see within range. A dart deals 1d4 + 1 force damage to its target. The darts all strike simultaneously, and you can direct them to hit one creature or several.\",\"duration\":\"Instantaneous\",\"higherLevels\":\"When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 2nd level or higher, the spell creates one more dart for each slot level above 1st.\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Magic Missile\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"120 feet\",\"school\":\"evocation\",\"type\":\"1st-level evocation\"}},{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"warlock, blood_hunter\",\"components\":\"V S M (Pickled octopus tentacle)\",\"description\":\"A 20-foot-radius void appears. It\\u0027s filled with whispers and slurping that can be heard up to 30 feet away. No light can illuminate the area, and creatures fully in it are blinded. The void\\u0027s area is difficult terrain. Any creature that starts its turn in the area takes 2d6 cold damage. Any creature that ends its turn there must pass a Dexterity save or take 2d6 acid damage.\",\"duration\":\"Concentration. Up to 1 minute\",\"higherLevels\":\"\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":3,\"name\":\"Hunger of Hadar\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"150 feet\",\"school\":\"conjuration\",\"type\":\"3rd-level conjuration\"}},{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"sorcerer, warlock, blood_hunter, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, S, M (a twig from a tree that has been struck by lightning)\",\"description\":\"A beam of crackling, blue energy lances out toward a creature within range, forming a sustained arc of lightning between you and the target. Make a ranged spell attack against that creature. On a hit, the target takes 1d12 lightning damage, and on each of your turns for the duration, you can use your action to deal 1d12 lightning damage to the target automatically. The spell ends if you use your action to do anything else. The spell also ends if the target is ever outside the spell\\u0027s range or if it has total cover from you.\",\"duration\":\"Concentration, up to 1 minute\",\"higherLevels\":\"When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 2nd level or higher, the damage increases by 1d12 for each slot level above 1st.\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Witch Bolt\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"30 feet\",\"school\":\"evocation\",\"type\":\"1st-level evocation\"}},{\"level\":3,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"bard, druid, sorcerer, warlock, blood_hunter, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, S\",\"description\":\"You attempt to charm a humanoid you can see within range. It must make a Wisdom saving throw, and does so with advantage if you or your companions are fighting it. If it fails the saving throw, it is charmed by you until the spell ends or until you or your companions do anything harmful to it. The charmed creature regards you as a friendly acquaintance. When the spell ends, the creature knows it was charmed by you.\",\"duration\":\"1 hour\",\"higherLevels\":\"When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 2nd level or higher, you can target one additional creature for each slot level above 1st. The creatures must be within 30 feet of each other when you target them.\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Charm Person\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"30 feet\",\"school\":\"enchantment\",\"type\":\"1st-level enchantment\"}},{\"level\":15,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"sorcerer, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, S\",\"description\":\"You create a 20-foot-radius sphere of poisonous, yellow-green fog centered on a point you choose within range. The fog spreads around corners. It lasts for the duration or until strong wind disperses the fog, ending the spell. Its area is heavily obscured.\\n\\nWhen a creature enters the spell\\u0027s area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, that creature must make a Constitution saving throw. The creature takes 5d8 poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Creatures are affected even if they hold their breath or don\\u0027t need to breathe.\\n\\nThe fog moves 10 feet away from you at the start of each of your turns, rolling along the surface of the ground. The vapors, being heavier than air, sink to the lowest level of the land, even pouring down openings.\",\"duration\":\"Concentration, up to 10 minutes\",\"higherLevels\":\"When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 6th level or higher, the damage increases by 1d8 for each slot level above 5th.\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":5,\"name\":\"Cloudkill\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"120 feet\",\"school\":\"conjuration\",\"type\":\"5th-level conjuration\"}},{\"level\":15,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"bard, sorcerer, warlock, blood_hunter, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, M (a snake\\u0027s tongue and either a bit of honeycomb or a drop of sweet oil)\",\"description\":\"You suggest a course of activity (limited to a sentence or two) and magically influence up to twelve creatures of your choice that you can see within range and that can hear and understand you. Creatures that can\\u0027t be charmed are immune to this effect. The suggestion must be worded in such a manner as to make the course of action sound reasonable. Asking the creature to stab itself, throw itself onto a spear, immolate itself, or do some other obviously harmful act automatically negates the effect of the spell.\\n\\nEach target must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, it pursues the course of action you described to the best of its ability. The suggested course of action can continue for the entire duration. If the suggested activity can be completed in a shorter time, the spell ends when the subject finishes what it was asked to do.\\n\\nYou can also specify conditions that will trigger a special activity during the duration. For example, you might suggest that a group of soldiers give all their money to the first beggar they meet. If the condition isn\\u0027t met before the spell ends, the activity isn’t performed.\\n\\nIf you or any of your companions damage a creature affected by this spell, the spell ends for that creature.\",\"duration\":\"24 hours\",\"higherLevels\":\"When you cast this spell using a 7th-level spell slot, the duration is 10 days. When you use an 8th-level spell slot, the duration is 30 days. When you use a 9th-level spell slot, the duration is a year and a day.\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":6,\"name\":\"Mass Suggestion\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"60 feet\",\"school\":\"enchantment\",\"type\":\"6th-level enchantment\"}},{\"level\":15,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"druid\",\"components\":\"V, S\",\"description\":\"This spell creates a magical link between a Large or larger inanimate plant within range and another plant, at any distance, on the same plane of existence. You must have seen or touched the destination plant at least once before. For the duration, any creature can step into the target plant and exit from the destination plant by using 5 feet of movement.\",\"duration\":\"1 round\",\"higherLevels\":\"\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":6,\"name\":\"Transport via Plants\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"10 feet\",\"school\":\"conjuration\",\"type\":\"6th-level conjuration\"}},{\"level\":15,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"sorcerer, fighter, rogue, wizard, bard\",\"components\":\"V\",\"description\":\"Choose an object that you can see within range. The object can be a door, a box, a chest, a set of Manacles, a padlock, or another object that contains a mundane or magical means that prevents access.\\n\\nA target that is held shut by a mundane lock or that is stuck or barred becomes unlocked, unstuck, or unbarred. If the object has multiple locks, only one of them is unlocked.\\n\\nIf you choose a target that is held shut with Arcane Lock, that spell is suppressed for 10 minutes, during which time the target can be opened and shut normally.\\n\\nWhen you cast the spell, a loud knock, audible from as far away as 300 feet, emanates from the target object\",\"duration\":\"Instantaneous\",\"higherLevels\":\"\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":2,\"name\":\"Knock\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"60 feet\",\"school\":\"transmutation\",\"type\":\"2nd-level transmutation\"}},{\"level\":15,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"sorcerer, fighter, rogue, wizard\",\"components\":\"V, S, M (a lodestone and a pinch of dust)\",\"description\":\"A thin green ray springs from your pointing finger to a target that you can see within range. The target can be a creature, an object, or a Creation of magical force, such as the wall created by Wall of Force.\\n\\nA creature targeted by this spell must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes 10d6+40 force damage. If this damage reduces the target to 0 Hit Points, it is disintegrated.\\n\\nA disintegrated creature and everything it is wearing and carrying, except Magic Items, are reduced to a pile of fine gray dust. The creature can be restored to life only by means of a True Resurrection or a wish spell.\\n\\nThis spell automatically disintegrates a Large or smaller nonmagical object or a Creation of magical force. If the target is a Huge or larger object or Creation of force, this spell disintegrates a 10-foot-cube portion of it. A magic item is unaffected by this spell\",\"duration\":\"Instantaneous\",\"higherLevels\":\"When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 7th level or higher, the damage increases by 3d6 for each slot level above 6th\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":6,\"name\":\"Disintegrate\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"60 feet\",\"school\":\"transmutation\",\"type\":\"6th-level transmutation\"}},{\"level\":15,\"spellModel\":{\"castingTime\":\"1 action\",\"classes\":\"druid\",\"components\":\"V, S, M (several seeds of any moonseed plant and a piece of opalescent feldspar)\",\"description\":\"A silvery beam of pale light shines down in a 5-foot-radius, 40-foot-high cylinder centered on a point within range. Until the spell ends, dim light fills the cylinder.\\n\\nWhen a creature enters the spell\\u0027s area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, it is engulfed in ghostly flames that cause searing pain, and it must make a Constitution saving throw. It takes 2d10 radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much on a successful one.\\n\\nA shapechanger makes its saving throw with disadvantage. If it fails, it also instantly reverts to its original form and can\\u0027t assume a different form until it leaves the spells light.\\n\\nOn each of your turns after you cast this spell use can use an action to move the beam 60 feet in any direction.\",\"duration\":\"Concentration, up to 1 minute\",\"higherLevels\":\"When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 3rd level or higher, the damage increases by 1d10 for each slot level above 2nd.\",\"isCustom\":false,\"isRitual\":false,\"jsonType\":\"spell\",\"level\":2,\"name\":\"Moonbeam\",\"notes\":\"\",\"pinned\":false,\"prepared\":false,\"range\":\"120 feet\",\"school\":\"evocation\",\"type\":\"2nd-level evocation\"}}],\"subtypes\":[],\"toolProficiencies\":[{\"hint\":\"\",\"level\":3,\"proficiency\":\"Qualquer Instrumento \"}],\"weaponProficiencies\":[]}],\"armorProficiencies\":[{\"hint\":\"\",\"level\":1,\"proficiency\":\"Light Armor\"},{\"hint\":\"\",\"level\":1,\"proficiency\":\"Medium Armor\"},{\"hint\":\"\",\"level\":1,\"proficiency\":\"Heavy Armor\"},{\"hint\":\"\",\"level\":1,\"proficiency\":\"Shields\"}],\"attacksByLevel\":[{\"amount\":2,\"level\":5},{\"amount\":3,\"level\":11},{\"amount\":4,\"level\":20},{\"amount\":1,\"level\":1}],\"baseAc\":10,\"classEquipment\":[{\"amountOfChoice\":1,\"equipmentsModels\":[{\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"Chain Mail\",\"number\":1},{\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"Leather Armor, Longbow and 20 Arrows\",\"number\":1}],\"id\":\"d4c43206-863e-47bf-a36d-a931ed7024e2\"},{\"amountOfChoice\":1,\"equipmentsModels\":[{\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"Martial Weapon and Shield\",\"number\":1},{\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"Martial Weapon\",\"number\":2}],\"id\":\"c1f2b5dc-ab0c-42d5-9593-70b4525d7f66\"},{\"amountOfChoice\":1,\"equipmentsModels\":[{\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"Light Crossbow and 20 bolts\",\"number\":1},{\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"Handaxe\",\"number\":2}],\"id\":\"3e2f2919-5225-4cb6-9e6c-425f563307d1\"},{\"amountOfChoice\":1,\"equipmentsModels\":[{\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"Dungeoneer\\u0027s Pack\",\"number\":1},{\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"Explorer\\u0027s Pack\",\"number\":1}],\"id\":\"72687f9e-7030-4b4a-b34c-72ef75b90154\"}],\"classSkills\":[{\"amountOfChoice\":2,\"id\":\"1749c005-5a4b-40e1-bd39-0e6ea64ace6e\",\"skills\":[{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{}],\"skillsModels\":[{\"name\":\"Acrobatics\",\"typeName\":\"SKILL\"},{\"name\":\"Animal Handling\",\"typeName\":\"SKILL\"},{\"name\":\"Athletics\",\"typeName\":\"SKILL\"},{\"name\":\"History\",\"typeName\":\"SKILL\"},{\"name\":\"Insight\",\"typeName\":\"SKILL\"},{\"name\":\"Intimidation\",\"typeName\":\"SKILL\"},{\"name\":\"Perception\",\"typeName\":\"SKILL\"},{\"name\":\"Survival\",\"typeName\":\"SKILL\"}]}],\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"ZERO\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You have a fighting style that grants you a feature\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom74cbee90-3569-4ac1-b610-2e1b724edfbe\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Fighting Style\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"On your turn, you can use a bonus action to regain hit points equal to 1d10 + your fighter level. Once you use this feature, you must finish a short or long rest before you can use it again\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Custom0769b185-23fd-43b6-9644-77bf45b8113b\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Second Wind\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"On your turn, you can take one additional action on top of your regular action and a possible bonus action. Once you use this feature, you must finish a short or long rest before you can use it again\",\"level\":2},{\"description\":\"On your turn, you can take one additional action on top of your regular action and a possible bonus action. Once you use this feature twice, you must finish a short or long rest before you can use it again. You can\\u0027t use it twice on the same turn\",\"level\":17}],\"id\":\"Customfa0b636c-2476-47d0-8a1b-55c5f286c0c6\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Action Surge\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":2},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You choose an archetype that you strive to emulate in your combat styles and techniques. It grants you a feature a 3rd level, and again at 7th, 10th, 15th, and 18th level\",\"level\":3}],\"id\":\"Customa566f2ed-c54b-4a00-8d5f-f352f4dc8b3b\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Martial Archetype\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":3},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can attack 2 times instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn\",\"level\":5},{\"description\":\"You can attack 3 times instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn\",\"level\":11},{\"description\":\"You can attack 4 times instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn\",\"level\":20}],\"id\":\"Customaa326561-317c-4229-a1af-5e323cd0e2fa\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Extra Attack\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":5},{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You can reroll a saving throw that you fail. If you do so, you must use the new roll. You shall use this feature 1 time between long rests\",\"level\":9},{\"description\":\"You can reroll a saving throw that you fail. If you do so, you must use the new roll. You shall use this feature 2 times between long rests\",\"level\":13},{\"description\":\"You can reroll a saving throw that you fail. If you do so, you must use the new roll. You shall use this feature 3 times between long rests\",\"level\":17}],\"id\":\"Customc0077d3d-a78f-4377-8a82-d1bf755a161b\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Indomitable\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":9}],\"hitDie\":\"D10\",\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Class\",\"multiclassArmor\":true,\"multiclassSkills\":false,\"multiclassTools\":false,\"multiclassWeapons\":true,\"name\":\"Fighter\",\"savingThrows\":{\"cha\":false,\"con\":true,\"dex\":false,\"intelligence\":false,\"str\":true,\"wis\":false},\"selectableFeatures\":[{\"amountsPerLevel\":[{\"amount\":1,\"level\":4}],\"availableFeatures\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"Whenever you reach a level in this class that grants the Ability Score Improvement feature, you can do one of the following, as you shift the focus of your martial practice:\\n\\n- Replace a fighting style you know with another fighting style available to fighters.\\n\\n- If you know any maneuvers from the Battle Master archetype, you can replace one maneuver you know with a different maneuver\",\"level\":4}],\"id\":\"Custom44d3e9c1-a8a8-4f6f-9801-1a7ad2f24b60\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Martial Versatility\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":4}],\"canReselect\":false,\"id\":\"c377fe58-5583-4c61-b12c-57b25a8ee001\",\"name\":\"Fighter Optional Features\",\"selectedFeatures\":[]}],\"shouldShowCompanion\":false,\"skillProficiencies\":[],\"specialAbilities\":[{\"abilityCalculators\":[],\"amountsPerLevel\":[{\"amount\":1,\"level\":9},{\"amount\":2,\"level\":13},{\"amount\":3,\"level\":17}],\"associatedValueName\":\"\",\"id\":\"a71d1d17-4962-49d6-8d81-e7fb20d4b2db\",\"name\":\"Indomitable Uses\",\"type\":\"BASIC\",\"usesLeft\":0}],\"spellSlots\":[],\"spellcastingAbility\":\"Intelligence\",\"spells\":[],\"subtypeSelectionLevel\":1,\"subtypes\":[{\"acModifier\":\"Dexterity\",\"armorProficiencies\":[],\"attacksByLevel\":[],\"baseAc\":10,\"classWeapon\":{\"abilityName\":\"Strength\",\"damageType\":\"Bludgeoning\",\"diceAmount\":1,\"diceTypeName\":\"D4\",\"name\":\"\"},\"effectiveCasterLevel\":\"PARENT\",\"features\":[{\"feat\":{\"descriptionModels\":[{\"description\":\"You gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls you make with ranged weapons\",\"level\":1}],\"id\":\"Customc7dd47ec-3883-42cd-9238-6614c2557f67\",\"isFeature\":true,\"jsonType\":\"feat\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Fighting Style: Archery\",\"notes\":\"\",\"type\":\"Feat\"},\"level\":1}],\"hpModifier\":\"Constitution\",\"id\":\"fighter_archery\",\"jsonType\":\"class\",\"languages\":[],\"modelType\":\"Subtype\",\"multiclassAr